{"id": "28", "question": "how to fix a door that won't lock", "gt": "To fix a door that won't lock, you can try the following steps based on the given passages:\n1. Close the door and attempt to lock it.\n2. If it doesn't lock, open the door and use a chisel to tap and pry off the door stop on the striker side of the jamb. Remove the top door stop as well.\n3. Place the door stop back on the jamb, aligning it 1/4 inch from its original location using the distinct line left behind.\n4. Nail the side and top pieces of the door stop back on.\n5. If the latch still doesn't catch, tighten the hinges first.\n6. Enlarge the latch hole in the jamb if necessary.\n7. Enlarge the strike plate hole or move the strike plate if the latch doesn't align with it.\n8. Ensure all the door's hinge screws are tight.\nFollowing these steps should help fix the door lock issue.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the lock cylinder for any signs of obstruction or damage. Check if the key is being inserted correctly and if the key is not bent or damaged.\nIf the lock cylinder appears to be in good condition, try lubricating it with a suitable lock lubricant to ensure smooth operation.\nIf lubrication does not resolve the issue, inspect the door lock strike for any signs of damage or misalignment. Adjust the strike if necessary, or replace it if it is worn out.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 24.615, "generation_time_seconds": 21.7897, "selection_time_seconds": 2.8176, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 6006, 3705, 311, 1490, 421, 432, 374, 10277, 26118, 448, 279, 5296, 16953, 13, 1416, 432, 374, 537, 26118, 11, 1931, 622, 432, 448, 279, 5296, 16953, 13, 151645], "logp_l