{"id": "139", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded. The block concept is followed, where assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are grouped together and considered as a single asset. The assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset, even if it is not used for business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nBased on the given passage, the treatment when an asset is discarded according to the Income Tax Act is not explicitly stated. To answer the question accurately, we need to refer to the specific provisions of the Income Tax Act, which are not provided in the given passage. Therefore, the information required to answer the question is not available in the given text.\nTo find the treatment for an asset discarded under the Income Tax Act, we need to consult the specific provisions of the Income Tax Act. The given passage does not provide this information, so we cannot determine the treatment based solely on the provided text.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 28.822, "generation_time_seconds": 25.6912, "selection_time_seconds": 3.1179, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3897, 21085, 1558, 537, 6644, 894, 1995, 911, 279, 6380, 315, 11770, 979, 807, 525, 43210, 438, 817, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 13, 15277, 11, 432, 374, 537, 3204, 311, 4226, 279, 3405, 3118, 389, 279, 2661, 199