{"id": "205", "question": "what is chard vegetable", "gt": "Chard is a vegetable that has large, fleshy but tender deep green leaves and thick, crisp stalks. It is similar to spinach but has a stronger, more assertive flavor. Fresh young chard can be used raw in salads, while mature chard leaves and stalks are typically cooked or sautéed. Chard is in the same subspecies as beetroot and is cultivated for leaf production. It can be harvested while the leaves are young and tender or after maturity when the stems are slightly tougher. Chard is perishable and should be stored in the refrigerator for a minimum amount of time.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. Identify the key elements of the question: \"what is chard vegetable.\"\n2. Determine the specific information needed to answer the question.\n3. Analyze the given passage to find relevant information.\n4. Extract and organize the information from the passage.\n5. Formulate an answer based on the extracted information.\n6. Review the answer to ensure it addresses all aspects of the question.\n7. Provide the final answer.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. Identify the key elements of the question: \"what is chard vegetable.\"\n2. Determine the specific information needed to answer the question.\n3. Analyze the given passage to find relevant information.\n4. Extract and organize the information from the passage.\n5. Formulate an answer based on the extracted information.\n6. Review the answer to ensure it addresses all aspects of the question.\n7. Provide the final answer.\n6. Review the answer to ensure it addresses all aspects of the question.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 32.513, "generation_time_seconds": 28.4065, "selection_time_seconds": 4.0975, "reco