: "success"}}
{"id": "214", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "To properly wash wine glasses, you should scrub them by hand as it's the safest cleaning method. First, lay a towel in the sink before filling it with hot water. Wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage. Use a small amount of detergent only where it's needed -- in the bottom of the glass and around the rim. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles. If hot water and mild detergent can’t get your glasses clean, use baking soda to remove any stubborn wine residue. Dissolve a small amount of soda with hot water and let it stand in the glass for a few minutes. The soda will dissolve any residual wine adhering to the glass. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem. After rinsing thoroughly with hot water, dry the wine glasses with a smooth lint-free cloth, such as a microfiber or flour sack towel.", "pred": "It is crucial to use the right cleaning solution because it prevents damage to the surface of the glass. The cleaning solution should be applied just before scrubbing, allowing a few seconds to penetrate and loosen any stuck-on residue. Over time, repeated use of the appropriate solution will keep the wine glasses looking pristine and prolong their lifespan.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "To wash wine glasses properly, a few materials and tools are necessary. First, a high-quality wine glass cleaner is essential. This cleaner should be used in conjunction with a soft, non-abrasive sponge. Additionally, a clean, warm water rinse is important to remove any remaining residue.\n\nThe recommended cleaning methods and techniques involve a gentle scrubbing motion with the non-abrasive sponge. Start by applying the wine glass cleaner evenly across the surface of the glass. Next, using the soft sponge, scrub the glass in a circular motion, ensuring that all sides, including the stem and bowl, are thoroughly cleaned. This helps to remove any wine stains or deposits that may have accumulated.\n\nIt is crucial to use the right cleaning solution because it prevents damage to the surface of the glass. The cleaning solution should be applied just before scrubbing, allowing a few seconds to penetrate and loosen any stuck-on residue. Over time, repeated use of the appropriate solution will keep the wine glasses looking pristine and prolong their lifespan.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Identify the materials and tools needed for washing wine glasses properly.\nStep 2: Determine the recommended cleaning methods and techniques for wine glasses.\nStep 3: Explain the importance of using the right cleaning solution and how it should be applied.\n\nTo wash wine glasses properly, a few materials and tools are necessary. First, a high-quality wine glass cleaner is essential. This cleaner should be used in conjunction with a soft, non-abrasive sponge. Additionally, a clean, warm water rinse is important to remove any remaining residue.\n\nThe recommended cleaning methods and techniques involve a gentle scrubbing motion with the non-abrasive sponge. Start by applying the wine glass cleaner evenly across the surface of the glass. Next, using the soft sponge, scrub the glass in a circular motion, ensuring that all sides, including the stem and bowl, are thoroughly cleaned. This helps to remove any wine stains or deposits that may have accumulated.\n\nIt is crucial to use the right cleaning solution because it prevents damage to the surface of the glass. The cleaning solution should be applied just before scrubbing, allowing a few seconds to penetrate and loosen any stuck-on residue. Over time, repeated use of the appropriate solution will keep the wine glasses looking pristine and prolong their lifespan.", "time_sec": 28.269, "generation_time_seconds": 25.184, "selection_time_seconds": 3.0782, "record_process": true, "