{"id": "286", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, start by preheating the oven to 325-350 degrees Fahrenheit. If you don't have time to defrost the roast, put it in the oven at 250 F for about an hour. Afterwards, take it out and season it with salt, pepper, and any seasonings you prefer, such as thyme, oregano or garlic. Rub the surface with 2 tsp. of olive oil. Place the roast in a roasting pan with the fat of the pork loin facing upwards, and put it back in the oven for about 1.5 to 3 hours depending on its size, or about 20-30 minutes per pound. Make sure the roast is cooked thoroughly by using a meat thermometer; the internal temperature should reach 150 degrees Fahrenheit. Once it is cooked, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe passage does not provide specific steps on how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, so I cannot generate the next logical reasoning step.\nThe passage does not provide specific steps on how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, so I cannot generate the next logical reasoning step.\nThe passage does not provide specific steps on how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, so I cannot generate the next logical reasoning step.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 21.313, "generation_time_seconds": 18.3349, "selection_time_seconds": 2.9674, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2661, 3405, 17064, 911, 1246, 311, 4296, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 13, 576, 3897, 21085, 1558, 537, 6644, 894, 3151, 11221, 389, 17233, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 5