{"id": "331", "question": "how to boil potatoes for easy peeling", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to boil potatoes for easy peeling:\n\n1. Bring a pot of water to a boil.\n2. Score your potatoes all the way around the center with a knife.\n3. Place your potatoes in the pot and boil for about 15 minutes or so.\n4. Prepare a bowl of ice water and place your potatoes in the water.\n5. Swish it around for a few seconds just enough so that it’s cool enough to handle.\n6. Remove your potato from the water and remove the skin.\n\nThe ice water bath helps to stop the cooking process and cool down the potatoes quickly, making the skin easier to peel off.", "pred": "[Boil potatoes for 20-30 minutes to ensure they are fully cooked but not overdone. If using a pressure cooker or steam method, this step can significantly reduce the time needed. Once cooked, allow the potatoes to cool for about 5-10 minutes before peeling. This cooling period helps to make the skin peel off more easily.]", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Based on the reasoning steps provided:\n\n1. **Determine the appropriate boiling time.** This step involves ensuring the potatoes are cooked fully but not overcooked. A general guideline is to boil them for 20-30 minutes, depending on the size of the potatoes. Smaller potatoes take less time than larger ones.\n\n2. **Use a pressure cooker or steam method for faster peeling.** While traditional boiling is fine, pressure cooking or steaming can speed up the peeling process by making the skin easier to remove. Pressure cooking involves sealing the potatoes in a pot and adding water to the bottom, then bringing it to a boil and reducing the heat to low pressure. Steam cooking involves placing the potatoes in a steamer basket and covering it, allowing the steam to cook the potatoes.\n\n3. **Cool the potatoes slightly before peeling.** Peeling is easier when the potatoes are not too hot. Allow the potatoes to cool for about 5-10 minutes once they are cooked. This helps to make the skin peel off more easily, especially if the potatoes were boiled in boiling water.\n\nAnswer:[Boil potatoes for 20-30 minutes to ensure they are fully cooked but not overdone. If using a pressure cooker or steam method, this step can significantly reduce the time needed. Once cooked, allow the potatoes to cool for about 5-10 minutes before peeling. This cooling period helps to make the skin peel off more easily.]", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\nThe reasoning steps are:\n- Determine the appropriate boiling time.\n- Use a pressure cooker or steam method for faster peeling.\n- Cool the potatoes slightly before peeling.\n\nBased on the reasoning steps provided:\n\n1. **Determine the appropriate boiling time.** This step involves ensuring the potatoes are cooked fully but not overcooked. A general guideline is to boil them for 20-30 minutes, depending on the size of the potatoes. Smaller potatoes take less time than larger ones.\n\n2. **Use a pressure cooker or steam method for faster peeling.** While traditional boiling is fine, pressure cooking or steaming can speed up the peeling process by making the skin easier to remove. Pressure cooking involves sealing the potatoes in a pot and adding water to the bottom, then bringing it to a boil and reducing the heat to low pressure. Steam cooking involves placing the potatoes in a steamer basket and covering it, allowing the steam to cook the potatoes.\n\n3. **Cool the potatoes slightly before peeling.** Peeling is easier when the potatoes are not too hot. Allow the potatoes to cool for about 5-10 minutes once they are cooked. This helps to make the skin peel off more easily, especially if the potatoes were boiled in boiling water.\n\nAnswer:[Boil potatoes for 20-30 minutes to ensure they are fully cooked but not overdone. If using a pressure cooker or steam method, this step can significantly reduce the time needed. Once cooked, allow the potatoes to cool for about 5-10 minutes before peeling. This cooling period helps to make the skin peel off more easily.]", "time_sec": 35.043, "generation_time_seconds": 31.9976, "selection_time_seconds": 3.0357, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 49837, 882, 323, 3015, 2213, 304, 279, 3338, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.6043, -0.1732, -0.0074, -2.0329, -0.4962, -0.7935, -0.516, -5.8793, -0.7602, -0.0024, -0.6938, -0.5415, -0.021, -29.7917, -22.8125, -12.1911, -5.9842, -20.625, -11.2194, -16.667, -11.3028, -10.2186, -11.0433, -8.2986, -7.8826, -7.9964, -8.7585, -8.3419, -7.5108, -8.1322, -7.7195, -6.3226, -5.509, -4.7187, -4.1232, -5.2496, -6.0639, -5.2984, -6.079, -4.8966, -5.873, -6.3378, -5.5067, -5.5767, -4.816, -5.5148, -5.4568, -6.8166, -6.5239, -5.4347, -4.5151, -5.6175, -5.6901, -5.3758, -5.3097, -4.6221, -4.008, -4.6429, -4.2858, -4.3764, -3.3176, -4.1336, -3.647, -4.6635, -3.8537, -3.6582, -3.647, -5.048, -4.4222, -6.2