{"id": "341", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is how you can make ribs:\n\nStep 1: Prepare the ribs\n\n* Remove the membrane from the bottom of the ribs (passage 3)\n* Season the ribs with a dry rub and mustard mixture (passage 2)\n\nStep 2: Grill the ribs\n\n* Heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium heat (passage 1)\n* Place the ribs meaty-side up on the grill and brush with some of the sauce (passage 1)\n* Cover the grill and cook for 5 minutes, then flip and brush the ribs with more sauce (passage 1)\n* Continue to cook and flip every 5 minutes, until the sauce has thickened and the ribs are heated through (passage 1)\n\nTotal grilling time: 20 minutes\n\nNote: The passages do not mention the temperature at which to cook the ribs, but a medium heat of 350°F to 450°F is suggested.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the main ingredients required for making ribs, such as pork ribs and seasonings.\nDetermine the cooking method, such as baking or grilling.\nExplain the preparation process for the ribs, which may include soaking, trimming, or marinating the ribs.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 16.092, "generation_time_seconds": 13.4329, "selection_time_seconds": 2.6507, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2661, 21085, 1558, 537, 6644, 894, 1995, 911, 1246, 311, 1281, 55149, 13, 15277, 11, 3118, 389, 279, 3897, 1467, 11, 358, 4157, 4226, 279, 3405, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.4538, -0.7032, -0.0413, -0.0312, -0.0, -1.8418, -0.2807, -0.2739, -0.2774, -0.1304, 0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0102, -1.9762, -0.0005, -2.8403, -0.0048, -0.0026, -1.0183, -1.7259, -0.0063, -0.9236, -0.1105, -0.3739, -0.0299, -0.0001, -1.429, -0.0411