{"id": "616", "question": "how to force removal of a printer in devices and printers", "gt": "To force removal of a printer in devices and printers:\n1. Use Print Manager or Printers folder to remove the printer or printer port.\n2. Close Print Manager or the Printers folder.\n3. Stop and restart the Spooler Service.\n4. Go to Control Panel > Hardware and Sound > Printers.\n5. Right-click the printer you want to remove and select Delete. If you cannot delete the printer, right-click it again, select Run as administrator, and then select Delete.\n6. If the printer is connected to the computer via USB cable, disconnect it from the printer.\n7. Turn off the printer and turn it back on again. Ensure that it is in a ready state.\n8. Remove the printer from the devices list and any associated Windows print drivers.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nLook for the printer in the list of devices and printers.\nLook for the printer in the list of devices and printers.\nLook for the printer in the list of devices and printers.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 24.159, "generation_time_seconds": 21.3096, "selection_time_seconds": 2.8404, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 7354, 476, 5413, 7481, 304, 279, 21085, 311, 4057, 264, 22380, 504, 279, 7611, 323, 55953, 1140, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 15