{"id": "631", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to guard a tall person in basketball\":\n\nTo guard a tall person in basketball, it's important to stay as close as possible to them when they're near the three-point line. Slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent and minimize shot opportunities. Additionally, keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player to defend against them effectively.", "pred": "To guard a tall person in basketball, focus on maintaining a low stance with bent knees and a straight back. Utilize quick, sidestepping movements to stay in front of the tall player and keep pace with them.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To guard a tall person in basketball, focus on maintaining a low stance with bent knees and a straight back. Utilize quick, sidestepping movements to stay in front of the tall player and keep pace with them.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n1. Identify the physical attributes of a tall person: Typically, a tall person in basketball has a longer wingspan and reach, which can give them an advantage in blocking shots and rebounding.\n2. Focus on defensive positioning: To guard a tall person, defenders should maintain a low stance, keeping their knees bent and back straight. This helps in maintaining balance and making it harder for the tall player to drive past.\n3. Utilize defensive footwork: Use quick, sidestepping movements to keep pace with the tall player, ensuring that you remain in front of them. This prevents them from easily outmaneuvering you.\n\nAnswer: To guard a tall person in basketball, focus on maintaining a low stance with bent knees and a straight back. Utilize quick, sidestepping movements to stay in front of the tall player and keep pace with them.", "time_sec": 25.807, "generation_time_seconds": 23.2114, "selection_time_seconds": 2.5868, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 11513, 16601, 553, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.1807, -0.0016, -0.0262, -0.0002, -0.8145, -0.0208, -2.7948, -2.7018, -0.0298, -0.116, -0.018, -0.3682, -0.0178, -0.0012, -2.113, -2.0788, -28.75, -26.25, -20.5209], "cumulative_logprob": -88.8043, "norm_logp": -4.6739, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 19, "avg_logp": -4.673911094665527}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 3151, 6961, 8201, 323, 7203, 12624, 315, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.1182, -0.0125, -0.0319, -1.4748, -0.8501, -0.091, -0.4314, -2.3269, -0.0043, -0.0034, -1.9807, -0.0004, -0.3748, -0.0374, -0.0029, -0.4016, -0.1404, -28.125, -25.4167], "cumulative_logprob": -64.8244, "norm_logp": -3.4118, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 19, "avg_logp": -3.4118099212646484}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 2, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 7361, 476, 12538, 429, 525, 16587, 369, 79500, 264, 16217, 1697, 304, 19240, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.7641, -0.0016, -0.0808, -0.4475, -2.8817, -2.0236, -0.1231, -0.2783, -0.2029, -3.834, -0.0042, -0.1958, -0.0088, -0.0055, -0.4431, -0.0191, -0.0, -0.0937, -0.0254], "cumulative_logprob": -12.4332, "norm_logp": -0.6544, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 19, "avg_logp": -0.6543863415718079}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 3, "token_ids": [2082, 55856, 279, 3151, 6961, 8201, 323, 7203, 12624, 315, 16217, 4217, 304, 19240, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.5557, -0.0, -0.0225, -2.0799, -0.409, -0.0774, -0.4351, -1.8655, -0.0021, -0.0061, -0.435, -0.0749, -0.1812, -0.0003, -0.4389, -0.0218, -27.2917, -21.1458, -16.3562], "cumulative_logprob": -72.3991, "norm_logp": -3.8105, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 19, "avg_logp": -3.810488700866699}]}, {"step": 0, "rollouts": [