{"id": "80", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "gt": "The cause of irritable bowel syndrome (IBS) is unknown. However, it is believed to be a result of abnormal gastrointestinal (GI) tract movements, increased awareness of bodily functions, disruption in communication between the brain and the GI tract, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances. Risk factors may include abnormal movements of the colon and small intestines (either too fast or slow, or too strong), hypersensitivity to pain from a full bowel or gas, and food sensitivities possibly caused by poor absorption of sugars or acids in food. Symptoms of IBS can include diarrhea, constipation, or alternating between the two, belly pains or cramps that worsen after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, as well as a lot of gas or bloating.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the specific symptoms mentioned in the passage related to IBS.\nIdentify the specific causes of IBS mentioned in the passage.\nCompare the identified symptoms and causes to known medical information about IBS to ensure accuracy.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 18.565, "generation_time_seconds": 15.7559, "selection_time_seconds": 2.8012, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [10380, 369, 3151, 1995, 911, 279, 13495, 323, 11137, 315, 358, 7347, 304, 279, 3897, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-5.5522, -0.0241, -0.304, -3.9545, -0.5592, -0.5159, -0.