{"id": "119", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek, American, Italian, and Spanish origin. In Greek and American, it means 'Reap; from Therasia.' In Italian, it is interpreted as 'Harvester.' In Spanish, the name is associated with two popular saints, 'Teresa of Avila' and 'Therese of Lisieux.' The name is also thought to originate from the Greek “therizein” meaning “to harvest, harvester” or from the Greek “theros” meaning “summer”.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe given passage does not provide information about the meaning of the name \"Teresa.\"\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nThe given passage does not provide information about the meaning of the name \"Teresa.\"\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 15.863, "generation_time_seconds": 13.1561, "selection_time_seconds": 2.7, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2661, 21085, 1558, 537, 3410, 1995, 911, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 63440, 13, 15277, 11, 358, 4157, 4226, 279, 3405, 1667, 1172, 279, 1995, 504, 279, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.8052, -1.2176, -0.0466, -0.0393, -0.0, -0.1229, -1.0839, -0.0249, -0.0003, -0.0191, -0.0016, -0.0017, -0.0, -0.3054, -0.0032, -1.8076, -0.0002, -0.7298, -0.0424, -0.2002, -0.0665, -0.0, -1.0663, -0.1197, -0.0031, -0.0028, -0.0671, -0.0077, -0.0422, -0.0351, -0.5091, -0.0147], "cumulative_logprob": -8.3862, "norm_logp": -0.2621, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 32, "avg_logp": -0.2620692849159241}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [785, 2661, 21085, 1558, 537, 3410, 1995, 911, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 330, 51, 37586, 1189, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151