{"id": "140", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that when an asset is discarded by a business but not sold, the Income Tax Act allows the scrap value of the asset to be deducted from the opening work-in-progress (WDV) of such asset in the previous year in which it was discarded. This reduction is taken into account while computing the depreciation expense for the subsequent years. However, any changes made to the value of the block must be made strictly in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of Income Tax Act 1961.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nLook for a specific section or clause in the Income Tax Act that discusses the disposal or scrapping of assets and the tax implications associated with it.\nLook for any specific examples, numbers, or comparisons in the Income Tax Act that clarify the treatment of assets when they are discarded.\nLook for any specific examples, numbers, or comparisons in the Income Tax Act that clarify the treatment of assets when they are discarded.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 22.751, "generation_time_seconds": 19.0834, "selection_time_seconds": 3.6578, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3897, 21085, 1558, 537, 6644, 894, 1995, 911, 279, 6380, 315, 11770, 979, 807, 525, 43210, 438, 817, 279, 7911, 3742, 1160, 13, 15277, 11, 358, 4157, 3410, 458, 4226, 3118, 389, 279, 2661, 1995, 13, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.7783, -3.4957, -0.6289, -0.027, -0.0, -0.02, -0.2969, -0.4356, -0.3936, -0.0056, -0.0025, -0.0296, -0.2099, -0.2552, -0.0351, 0.0, -0.0, -0.6304, -0.0, -0.0811, -1.6678, -0.0, -0.001, -0.0012, -0.8752, -0.0002, 