{"id": "193", "question": "how to attach multiple picture frames together", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some steps for attaching multiple picture frames together:\n\nPassage 1: Table-Stand Grouping\nTo join two or three frames together, you can use identical frames or one larger frame as the middle piece. Place the frames beside each other to see if you like the effect, and then mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nPassage 2: Hanging Multiple Pictures Together\nBefore attaching the frames together, test different arrangements of the group of multiple pictures on the floor. Once you have decided on the layout, screw the frames to the backer board, repeating the process for each frame. Attach a hanging wire to the back of the frames and hang them on the wall to enjoy the finished result.\n\nPassage 3: Attaching Frames Together\nTo attach two frames together, place them back to back and mark the hinge placement on the connecting sides. The placement should be the same distance from the bottom edge of each frame to ensure stability when the grouped pictures are placed on a table. Attach two small hinges to the marked areas to join the frames together.\n\nIn conclusion, the recommended method for attaching multiple picture frames together involves using identical or matching frames, marking the hinge placement on the connecting sides, and attaching small hinges to join the frames together. It's also important to test different arrangements of the group of pictures on the floor before attaching the frames together, and to ensure that the frames are securely attached to the backer board before hanging them on the wall.", "pred": "To attach multiple picture frames together, you will need the following materials and hardware:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To attach multiple picture frames together, you will need the following materials and hardware:\n\n1. Picture frames (at least two)\n2. Picture frame adhesive (such as spray adhesive or glue)\n3. Clear tape\n4. Measuring tape\n5. Pencil\n6. Screwdriver (if using screws)\n\nThe process of measuring and preparing the frames for attachment is as follows:\n\n1. Measure the dimensions of each picture frame to ensure they are compatible in size and shape.\n2. Mark the desired attachment points on the frames using a pencil and the measuring tape.\n3. Apply the picture frame adhesive to the marked attachment points, making sure to cover the entire area for a secure bond.\n4. If using screws, insert them into the pre-drilled holes at the marked attachment points.\n5. Once the adhesive is applied or the screws are in place, attach the frames together by aligning them at the marked attachment points.\n6. Use clear tape to reinforce the attachment and ensure the frames are securely joined.\n\nIt's important to note that the specific type of hardware and materials may vary depending on the frames and the desired level of attachment strength. Always follow the manufacturer's instructions for the best results.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnderstand the materials and hardware needed for attaching multiple picture frames together.\nDetermine the specific type of hardware and materials required for attaching the frames together.\nDescribe the process of measuring and preparing the frames for attachment.\n\nAnswer: To attach multiple picture frames together, you will need the following materials and hardware:\n\n1. Picture frames (at least two)\n2. Picture frame adhesive (such as spray adhesive or glue)\n3. Clear tape\n4. Measuring tape\n5. Pencil\n6. Screwdriver (if using screws)\n\nThe process of measuring and preparing the frames for attachment is as follows:\n\n1. Measure the dimensions of each picture frame to ensure they are compatible in size and shape.\n2. Mark the desired attachment points on the frames using a pencil and the measuring tape.\n3. Apply the picture frame adhesive to the marked attachment points, making sure to cover the entire area for a secure bond.\n4. If using screws, insert them into the pre-drilled holes at the marked attachment points.\n5. Once the adhesive is applied or the screws are in place, attach the frames together by aligning them at the marked attachment points.\n6. Use clear tape to reinforce the attachment and ensure the frames are securely joined.\n\nIt's important to note that the specific type of hardware and materials may vary depending on the frames and the desired level of attachment strength. Always follow the manufacturer's instructions for the best results.", "time_sec": 28.12, "generation_time_seconds": 25.319, "selection_time_seconds": 2.791, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [3838, 7236, 525, 4362, 369, 71808, 5248, 6802, 14087, 3786, 30, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-3.6031, -0.811, -0.5698, -1.2317, -1.5026, -0.001, -0.0569, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0036, -0.0028, -0.0001, -28.3333, -21.0417, -11.7715, -14.377, -8.6558, -12.7092, -9.7986, -8.3533, -8.978, -8.3628, -7.598, -7.4122, -5.9371, -5.951, -5.7662, -6.1491, -5.6927, -5.9004, -4.7749, -5.3394, -4.6871, -5.3412, -5.226, -4.5636, -4.2276, -3.6061, -3.9261, -5.4103], "cumulative_logprob": -237.6728, "norm_logp": -5.9418, "input_len": 140, "output_tokens": 40, "avg_logp": -5.941826820373535}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [2082, 55856, 279, 7236, 323, 7375, 2567, 369, 71808, 6802, 14087, 3786, 13, 1096, 2578, 2924, 64458, 11, 33639, 11773, 11, 476, 3281, 26111, 6188, 369, 6802, 4034, 14614, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], 