{"id": "287", "question": "how to cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven", "gt": "To cook a frozen pork loin roast in the oven, preheat the oven to 325 degrees F. Place the frozen roast in a roasting pan and rub the surface with olive oil and season with salt, pepper, and desired seasonings. Place the roast, uncovered, in the preheated oven. Cook for about 20-30 minutes per pound or until the internal temperature reaches 150 degrees F. Once cooked, cover the roast with aluminum foil and let it sit for 30 minutes before serving.", "pred": "Preheat the oven to the appropriate temperature, season the pork loin roast with salt, pepper, or other herbs and spices, and then place it in the oven to cook.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Preheat the oven to the appropriate temperature, season the pork loin roast with salt, pepper, or other herbs and spices, and then place it in the oven to cook.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nInspect the pork loin roast for any signs of thawing or browning, and ensure it is evenly distributed across the baking tray if using one.\nThe next logical step would be to preheat the oven to the appropriate temperature according to the recipe or cooking instructions.\nApply a seasoning such as salt, pepper, or other herbs and spices to the pork loin roast to enhance its flavor.\n\nAnswer: Preheat the oven to the appropriate temperature, season the pork loin roast with salt, pepper, or other herbs and spices, and then place it in the oven to cook.", "time_sec": 30.635, "generation_time_seconds": 27.2031, "selection_time_seconds": 3.4236, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 17975, 323, 17233, 11221, 369, 264, 19690, 35067, 76960, 57685, 1730, 304, 279, 21085, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 15