{"id": "491", "question": "how can you tell who liked your tweet", "gt": "You can tell who liked your tweet by using websites such as Favotter.net and Favstar.fm, or by going to Twitter.com and logging in with your Twitter username and password. Once logged in, click on your Twitter name, located on the upper right hand corner of your account's Home page, then click on Settings and finally Blue Notifications link at the top of the screen. By setting this feature, you will receive an email notification whenever someone marks one of your tweets as one of their favorites.", "pred": "To determine who liked your tweet, you can use the following steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To determine who liked your tweet, you can use the following steps:\n1. Open the social media platform where your tweet was posted (e.g., Twitter).\n2. Locate your tweet in your feed or search results.\n3. Click on the \"likes\" or \"likes count\" icon below your tweet.\n4. The list of usernames who liked your tweet will be displayed.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo determine who liked your tweet, you can use the following steps:\n1. Open the social media platform where your tweet was posted (e.g., Twitter).\n2. Locate your tweet in your feed or search results.\n3. Click on the \"likes\" or \"likes count\" icon below your tweet.\n4. The list of usernames who liked your tweet will be displayed.\nThe next logical reasoning step is to click on the username of a specific user to see their profile and potentially follow them.\nTo determine who liked your tweet, you can use the following steps:\n1. Open the social media platform where your tweet was posted (e.g., Twitter).\n2. Locate your tweet in your feed or search results.\n3. Click on the \"likes\" or \"likes count\" icon below your tweet.\n4. The list of usernames who liked your tweet will be displayed.\nThe next logical reasoning step is to click on the username of a specific user to see their profile and potentially follow them.\n\nAnswer: To determine who liked your tweet, you can use the following steps:\n1. Open the social media platform where your tweet was posted (e.g., Twitter).\n2. Locate your tweet in your feed or search results.\n3. Click on the \"likes\" or \"likes count\" icon below your tweet.\n4. The list of usernames who liked your tweet will be displayed.", "time_sec": 30.211, "generation_time_seconds": 27.0508, "selection_time_seconds": 3.1497, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 8253, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 11, 498, 646, 990, 279, 2701, 7354, 510, 16, 13, 5264, 279, 3590, 3687, 5339, 1380, 697, 11809, 572, 8454, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 6271, 4292, 17, 13, 95210, 697, 11809, 304, 697, 5395, 476, 2711, 3059, 624, 18, 13, 9189, 389, 279, 330, 25039, 1, 476, 330, 25039, 1760, 1, 4603, 3685, 697, 11809, 624, 19, 13, 576, 1140, 315, 82051, 879, 14915, 697, 11809, 686, 387, 12596, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.1868, -0.1517, -0.2025, -0.0001, -0.0354, -0.0, -0.0062, -0.0972, -2.7231, -2.336, -0.1166, -0.2765, -0.3545, -3.2613, -0.0115, -0.0, -1.2896, -0.3426, -3.1604, -0.0001, -0.0012, -0.0091, -0.5698, -0.0, -0.1177, -0.0009, -1.3041, -0.0115, -0.0, -0.0036, -0.0, -0.6976, -0.0, 0.0, -0.5643, -0.2146, -0.0048, -0.4734, -1.0548, -0.8147, -0.0088, -0.3371, -3.3693, -0.0048, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0473, -0.001, -0.0433, -1.3063, -0.9837, -0.0, -0.6779, -0.0015, -0.3362, -0.2026, -0.0, -0.263, -1.9948, -0.0653, -0.0, -0.9939, -0.0016, 0.0, -0.7438, -0.1592, -0.0003, -1.2525, -0.2628, -0.0527, -0.0125, -0.0, -0.019, -0.2094, -0.0001, -0.5689, -0.4731], "cumulative_logprob": -35.7869, "norm_logp": -0.4648, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 77, "avg_logp": -0.4647700786590576}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [10380, 369, 279, 2112, 4488, 3137, 389, 279, 11809, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645,