{"id": "39", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, you can run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. Be careful not to damage the dryer's interior. You can then apply 1 to 2 tsp. of nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Afterward, rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover. You can mix 1 tsp. of liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water, dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water. Some plastic may be extremely difficult to remove, in which case you can try heating the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun and then peel it off. If not all plastic comes off, you may need to replace the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nLook for instructions or warnings related to dryer maintenance in the user manual or on the dryer's label.\nLook for specific sections or paragraphs that discuss cleaning or maintenance, particularly those related to the dryer drum or lint screen.\nLook for specific methods or techniques mentioned for cleaning the dryer drum or lint screen, such as using a vacuum cleaner, a dryer cleaner brush, or a dryer cleaning tool.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 20.003, "generation_time_seconds": 17.0307, "selection_time_seconds": 2.9639, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 12188, 3589, 429, 525, 15700, 304, 279, 46622, 13, 4220, 1410, 2924, 2513, 1075, 12188, 17899, 11, 12188, 23853, 11, 476, 2613, 12188, 5479, 504, 14346, 7611, 382, 1