{"id": "49", "question": "how to fold a quilt", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here are the steps to fold a quilt:\n\n1. Lay the quilt on a flat surface.\n2. Fold the lower right corner up towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n3. Fold the lower left corner up towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n4. Fold the top left corner down towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n5. Fold the top right corner down towards the center of the quilt, making sure the fold is on the bias.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question \"How to fold a quilt\" can be summarized in five steps:\n\n1. Lay the quilt flat.\n2. Fold lower right corner up.\n3. Fold lower left corner up.\n4. Fold top left corner down.\n5. Fold top right corner down.", "pred": "To fold a quilt, start by identifying the type and size of the quilt. Lay it out flat on a large, flat surface. Fold the quilt in half lengthwise, aligning the edges. Smooth out wrinkles and creases. Fold it in half again widthwise, aligning the edges. Fold it one more time diagonally to create a smaller, more compact shape. Smooth out any remaining wrinkles and creases. Pin or tape the quilt to keep the folds in place. Finally, carefully lift the folded quilt and place it on a hanger or a quilt rack to store or display it.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To fold a quilt, start by identifying the type and size of the quilt. Lay it out flat on a large, flat surface. Fold the quilt in half lengthwise, aligning the edges. Smooth out wrinkles and creases. Fold it in half again widthwise, aligning the edges. Fold it one more time diagonally to create a smaller, more compact shape. Smooth out any remaining wrinkles and creases. Pin or tape the quilt to keep the folds in place. Finally, carefully lift the folded quilt and place it on a hanger or a quilt rack to store or display it.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Identify the type of quilt and its size.\nStep 2: Lay out the quilt flat on a large, flat surface.\nStep 3: Fold the quilt in half lengthwise, aligning the edges.\nStep 4: Smooth out any wrinkles and creases in the folded quilt.\nStep 5: Fold the quilt in half again, this time widthwise, aligning the edges.\nStep 6: Fold the quilt in half one more time, this time diagonally, creating a smaller, more compact shape.\nStep 7: Smooth out any remaining wrinkles and creases.\nStep 8: Pin or\nStep 8: Pin or tape the quilt to keep the folds in place.\nStep 9: Carefully lift the folded quilt and place it on a hanger or a quilt rack to store or display it.\n\nAnswer: To fold a quilt, start by identifying the type and size of the quilt. Lay it out flat on a large, flat surface. Fold the quilt in half lengthwise, aligning the edges. Smooth out wrinkles and creases. Fold it in half again widthwise, aligning the edges. Fold it one more time diagonally to create a smaller, more compact shape. Smooth out any remaining wrinkles and creases. Pin or tape the quilt to keep the folds in place. Finally, carefully lift the folded quilt and place it on a hanger or a quilt rack to store or display it.", "time_sec": 32.096, "generation_time_seconds": 28.3907, "selection_time_seconds": 3.6897, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 943, 315, 60736, 323, 1181, 1379, 624, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 43924, 700, 279, 60736, 10063, 389, 264, 3460, 11, 10063, 7329, 624, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 60473, 279, 60736, 304, 4279, 3084, 4482, 11, 5285, 287, 279, 12822, 624, 8304, 220, 19, 25, 50725, 700, 894, 73107, 323, 1884, 2264, 304, 279, 47035, 60736, 624, 8304, 220, 20, 25, 60473, 279, 60736, 304, 4279, 1549, 11, 419, 882, 2374, 4482, 11, 5285, 287, 279, 12822, 624, 8304, 220, 21, 25, 60473, 279, 60736, 304, 4279, 825, 803, 882, 11, 419, 882, 84018, 745, 11,