.33, "GAVIE-Rel": 0.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 0.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "82", "question": "symptoms and causes of ibs", "gt": "Symptoms of irritable bowel syndrome include diarrhea (often described as violent episodes of diarrhea), constipation, constipation alternating with diarrhea, belly pains or cramps, usually in the lower half of the belly, that get worse after meals and feel better after a bowel movement, and a lot of gas or bloating. Causes of irritable bowel syndrome are unknown but it is believed to be due to a number of factors including alteration in gastrointestinal (GI) tract motility, abnormal nervous system signals, increased sensitivity to pain, and food intolerances.", "pred": "Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, changes in bowel habits, and diarrhea or constipation. Causes can include diet, stress, and genetics. For example, dairy products and high-fiber foods can exacerbate symptoms of abdominal pain and bloating.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Symptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, changes in bowel habits, and diarrhea or constipation. Causes can include diet, stress, and genetics. For example, dairy products and high-fiber foods can exacerbate symptoms of abdominal pain and bloating.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nProvide specific examples of symptoms associated with IBS, such as abdominal pain, bloating, and changes in bowel habits.\nProvide a brief explanation of the causes of IBS, including factors such as diet, stress, and genetics.\nExplain how each symptom, such as abdominal pain and bloating, can be exacerbated by specific dietary triggers like dairy products or high-fiber foods.\n\nSymptoms of IBS include abdominal pain, bloating, changes in bowel habits, and diarrhea or constipation. Causes can include diet, stress, and genetics. For example, dairy products and high-fiber foods can exacerbate symptoms of abdominal pain and bloating.", "time_sec": 28.403, "generation_time_seconds": 26.10