{"id": "103", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The various systems in the human body work together to ensure its normal functioning. For instance, the urinary system works with all other systems to clean the blood by removing waste products from the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. This includes organs like the kidneys and lower intestines. Similarly, the respiratory system also collaborates with all other systems to provide oxygen to all body parts and remove carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems. The respiratory system comprises the nose, larynx, trachea, and lungs.", "pred": "The body systems work together through a complex network of interactions and feedback mechanisms. For example, the digestive system works in conjunction with the circulatory system to transport nutrients to cells, while the respiratory system works in tandem with the circulatory system to deliver oxygen to the body's tissues.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: The body systems work together through a complex network of interactions and feedback mechanisms. For example, the digestive system works in conjunction with the circulatory system to transport nutrients to cells, while the respiratory system works in tandem with the circulatory system to deliver oxygen to the body's tissues.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe body systems work together through a complex network of interactions and feedback mechanisms. For example, the digestive system works in conjunction with the circulatory system to transport nutrients to cells, while the respiratory system works in tandem with the circulatory system to deliver oxygen to the body's tissues.\nThe body systems work together through a complex network of interactions and feedback mechanisms. For example, the digestive system works in conjunction with the circulatory system to transport nutrients to cells, while the respiratory system works in tandem with the circulatory system to deliver oxygen to the body's tissues.\nThe body systems work together through a complex network of interactions and feedback mechanisms. For example, the digestive system works in conjunction with the circulatory system to transport nutrients to cells, while the respiratory system works in tandem with the circulatory system to deliver oxygen to the body's tissues.\n\nAnswer: The body systems work together through a complex network of interactions and feedback mechanisms. For example, the digestive system works in conjunction with the circulatory system to transport nutrients to cells, while the respiratory system works in tandem with the circulatory system to deliver oxygen to the body's tissues.", "time_sec": 31.712, "generation_time_seconds": 28.4403, "selection_time_seconds": 3.2602, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2487, 5942, 975, 3786, 1526, 264, 6351, 3922, 315, 21880, 323, 11055, 23783, 13, 1752, 3110, 11, 279, 58971, 1849, 4278, 304, 31446, 448, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 7557, 36393, 311, 7761, 11, 1393, 279, 41531, 1849, 4278, 304, 65942, 448, 279, 4225, 37120, 1849, 311, 6359, 23552, 311, 279, 2487, 594, 38781, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.6763, -2.1306, -0.0105, -0.0227, -0.0001, -0.3218, -0.2828, -0.669, -0.1103, -0.0004, -0.0658, -0.2817, -0.1046, -0.361, -0.2571, -0.2197, -0.0963, -0.0003, -0.0012, -1.6361, -0.0042, -0.8485, -0.1292, -0.0749, 0.0, -0.0, -0.388, 0.0, -0.1755, -0.0152, -0.1239, -0.0057, -1.5843, -0.6195, -1.5591, -0.5163, -0.0002, -0.0604, -0.0007, -2.2957, -1.7404, -0.3532, -0.0125, -0.0001, -0.5964, 0.0, -0.0232, -0.0001, -0.2231, -0.0, -0.3736, -0.8613, -0.2841, -0.9837, -0.0091, -0.0546, -2.783