{"id": "112", "question": "what is the difference between the leeward and windward islands?", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the main difference between the Windward Islands and the Leeward Islands is their exposure to the northeast trade winds (northeasterlies). The Windward Islands are exposed to the wind and are therefore wetter and receive more rainfall, while the Leeward Islands are away from the wind and are drier, but still receive some rainfall. Additionally, the Windward Islands are located southeast of the Caribbean Sea, while the Leeward Islands are located northwest of the Caribbean Sea.", "pred": "The leeward and windward islands differ in their exposure to the trade winds. The leeward islands are positioned to the leeward (downwind) side of the trade winds, experiencing more rainfall and less direct exposure to the trade winds. In contrast, the windward islands are positioned to the windward (upwind) side of the trade winds, resulting in drier conditions and greater exposure to the trade winds.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "The leeward and windward islands differ in their exposure to the trade winds. The leeward islands are positioned to the leeward (downwind) side of the trade winds, experiencing more rainfall and less direct exposure to the trade winds. In contrast, the windward islands are positioned to the windward (upwind) side of the trade winds, resulting in drier conditions and greater exposure to the trade winds.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning step involves identifying the key geographical features or characteristics that distinguish the leeward and windward islands. The leeward islands are those that lie to the leeward (downwind) side of the trade winds, while the windward islands are those that are to the windward (upwind) side of the trade winds. This difference in location relative to the trade winds leads to distinct environmental and climatic conditions on each side. For example, the leeward islands tend to have more rainfall and less exposure to the trade winds, while the windward islands are more directly exposed to the trade winds, leading to drier conditions and less\nThe next logical reasoning step is to analyze the specific environmental and climatic conditions that result from the leeward and windward positions of the islands relative to the trade winds. This will help in understanding the differences in rainfall, temperature, and overall climate between the two types of islands.\nThe next logical reasoning step is to examine the specific environmental and climatic conditions that result from the leeward and windward positions of the islands relative to the trade winds. This will help in understanding the differences in rainfall, temperature, and overall climate between the two types of islands.\n\nThe leeward and windward islands differ in their exposure to the trade winds. The leeward islands are positioned to the leeward (downwind) side of the trade winds, experiencing more rainfall and less direct exposure to the trade winds. In contrast, the windward islands are positioned to the windward (upwind) side of the trade winds, resulting in drier conditions and greater exposure to the trade winds.", "time_sec": 42.621, "generation_time_seconds": 39.2087, "selection_time_seconds": 3.4004, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 52901, 4419, 315, 279, 512, 24035, 323, 9956, 1606, 29000, 311, 3535, 279, 12158, 11799, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645