{"id": "120", "question": "teresa name meaning", "gt": "The name Teresa is of Greek origin and means \"Reap; from Therasia\" or \"Harvester\". It is also a Spanish and Italian name and is associated with two popular saints, Teresa of Avila and Therese of Lisieux. The name Theresa is a variation of Teresa and also means \"Reaper; from Therasia\". The etymology of the name is uncertain, but it is thought to come from the Greek words \"therizein\" meaning \"to harvest, harvester\" or \"theros\" meaning \"summer\".", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe passages do not provide information about the meaning of the name Teresa.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nThe passages do not provide information about the meaning of the name Teresa.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 19.944, "generation_time_seconds": 16.7242, "selection_time_seconds": 3.2102, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 2266, 315, 279, 3405, 624, 785, 3405, 17064, 911, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 63440, 382], "logp_list": [-2.3677, -0.0027, -0.0132, -0.0004, -0.1121, -0.0055, -2.7522, -0.1775, -0.0007, -0.0172, -0.5415, -0.0246, -0.0125, -0.9245, -0.0963, -0.0001, -0.009, -0.0002, -0.0011, -0.0, -1.1995, -0.219], "cumulative_logprob": -8.4775, "norm_logp": -0.3853, "input_len": 137, "output_tokens": 22, "avg_logp": -0.3853517174720764}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [785, 46769, 653, 537, 3410, 1995, 911, 279, 7290, 315, 279, 829, 63440, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.8052, -2.6759, -0.8387, -0.0, -0.1545, -0.5773, -0.0544, -0.0006, -0.013, -0.0031, -0.0039, -0.0, -0.1763, -0.0025, -0.0318, -34.0625, -28.75, -18.