{"id": "141", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nAccording to passage 1, when an asset is discarded by the business but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which such asset is discarded. This reduction is allowed under section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act.\n\nPassage 3 further states that the assessee is entitled to claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even though such discarded asset is not used for the purposes of business or profession in such year and subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment when an asset is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the block value of the asset by the scrap value in the previous year in which it is discarded, and to claim depreciation on the residual value of the asset in the year of discard and subsequent years.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nBased on the given question, it is asking about the treatment of an asset when it is discarded according to the Income Tax Act. The first logical step is to identify the relevant section or provision of the Income Tax Act that pertains to the disposal of assets.\nThe next logical step is to review the specific section of the Income Tax Act that deals with the disposal of assets and the treatment of such disposal for tax purposes. This involves identifying the relevant clauses or sections that address the taxation of asset discarding or disposal.\nOnce the relevant section of the Income Tax Act is identified, the next logical step is to analyze the specific provisio