{"id": "216", "question": "how to wash wine glasses properly", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are the steps to properly wash wine glasses:\n\n1. If hot water and mild detergent cannot remove wine residue, use baking soda to dissolve and loosen the adhesive residue (Passage 1).\n2. To clean the inside of a glass, use a stemware brush with soft-foam bristles and rinse thoroughly with hot water (Passage 2).\n3. For hand cleaning, lay a towel in the sink before filling with hot water and wash one wine glass at a time to avoid damage (Passage 3). Use a small amount of detergent and only in the bottom of the glass and around the rim to avoid flavoring future wine. Cradle the bowl of the glass in one hand while washing to protect the stem.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the material of the wine glasses to determine the appropriate cleaning method.\nLook for any specific instructions or warnings on the wine glasses regarding cleaning, such as avoiding certain cleaners or methods.\nIdentify the type of stains on the wine glasses to apply the correct cleaning techniques.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 20.444, "generation_time_seconds": 17.448, "selection_time_seconds": 2.9858, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 943, 315, 13078, 28147, 25, 33396, 4494, 315, 28147, 11, 1741, 438, 64293, 1320, 2095, 11, 13078, 15394, 70378, 11, 323, 13078, 28147, 11, 1231, 1373, 10078, 2155, 15826, 5413, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 1516