{"id": "375", "question": "what is dmso used for", "gt": "DMSO, or dimethyl sulfoxide, is used in a variety of ways both industrially and medically. Industrially, it is used as an antifreeze and a solvent for numerous chemicals. Medically, DMSO is applied to the skin as an anti-inflammatory and general pain reliever, most commonly for muscles and joints. It is also used to promote healing for minor cuts, burns, soft tissue damage, local tissue death, and skin ulcers. DMSO has the unique ability to penetrate skin and tissue, allowing it to enter the bloodstream.", "pred": "DMSO is used in various applications such as in the field of chemistry, as a solvent or reagent, in the field of medicine, as an antifreeze agent, and in the field of industry, as a lubricant and cleaning agent.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: DMSO is used in various applications such as in the field of chemistry, as a solvent or reagent, in the field of medicine, as an antifreeze agent, and in the field of industry, as a lubricant and cleaning agent.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the specific uses of DMSO as described in the passages.\nIdentify the specific applications or uses of DMSO mentioned in the given passages.\nAnalyze the context of each use of DMSO to determine its purpose or benefit.\n\nAnswer: DMSO is used in various applications such as in the field of chemistry, as a solvent or reagent, in the field of medicine, as an antifreeze agent, and in the field of industry, as a lubricant and cleaning agent.", "time_sec": 21.261, "generation_time_seconds": 18.5276, "selection_time_seconds": 2.7239, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 6813, 315, 279, 3405, 624, 785, 3405, 17064, 911, 279, 5711, 315, 422, 4826, 46, 11, 892, 13352, 369, 8126, 41872, 25774, 15011, 577, 382], "logp_list": [-2.7