{"id": "405", "question": "2006 chevy remove door panel", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is the answer to the question:\n\nTo remove the rear door panel in a 2006 Chevy HHR, you should follow these steps:\n\n1. Remove the two screws located inside the door pull cup.\n2. Remove the screw located in the middle of the inside door handle.\n3. Remove the pin on the outer edge of the door that holds the panel in place.\n4. Use a door panel removal tool to pry the door panel off of the HHR rear door.\n\nIt is important to note that an instructional video is also available that shows the entire process and location of the screws and pin.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe given passage does not provide any information about the process of removing a door panel from a 2006 Chevrolet vehicle. Therefore, the current step cannot be completed as there is no relevant information to analyze.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nThe given passage mentions \"2006 chevrolet remove door panel,\" but it does not provide any specific instructions or details on how to remove the door panel. Therefore, there is insufficient information to provide a step-by-step guide on the process of removing the door panel.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 22.26, "generation_time_seconds": 19.087, "selection_time_seconds": 3.1653, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 17, 25, 64547, 279, 3151, 7375, 4362, 311, 4057, 279, 6006, 6945, 504, 279, 220, 17, 15, 15, 21, 42377, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645,