{"id": "580", "question": "what do i do if i got my sperrys wet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, if your Sperry shoes get wet, it is recommended to use a leather conditioner to help revitalize the leather and infuse moisture back into it. This is especially important if you wash your shoes with detergent, as it tends to dry out the leather. If you don't have a leather conditioner on hand, you can use a suede bar or leather brush to clean the shoes. It's best to avoid getting light tan Sperry shoes wet, as water might stain them. However, if you do get them wet, using a suede bar or leather brush should help remove any stains.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Determine the type of wetness. Is it just a light splash or is the shoe completely saturated?\nStep 2: Assess the shoe's material. Are the Sperrys made of waterproof or water-resistant material?\nStep 3: Check the condition of the shoe. Is there visible damage to the shoe, such as the sole or upper part being torn or discolored?\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 30.447, "generation_time_seconds": 26.4048, "selection_time_seconds": 4.0296, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [40, 1184, 311, 37163, 279, 943, 315, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 21085, 311, 10354, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.9648, -1.526, -1.5073, -3.0676, -0.5684, -1.2895, -0.0013, -1.4575, -2.1533, -0.0782, -0.0002, -1.1458, -0.301, -1.2903, -0.5435, -0.2324, -27.9167, -23.9583, -8.3464, -16.66