{"id": "641", "question": "differences and similarities between red and white blood cells", "gt": "Both red blood cells (RBCs) and white blood cells (WBCs) are found in the blood and are part of the circulatory system. They are both formed from pluripotent stem cells in the red bone marrow and contain cell membranes and cytoplasm. The main difference is their functions. RBCs are responsible for delivering oxygen from the lungs to the tissue in the body, while WBCs are part of the immune system and help the body combat diseases, viruses, etc.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\nBased on the given passage, the answer is \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. The passage does not provide any information about the differences or similarities between red and white blood cells.\n2. The question asks for specific details about these cells, which are not present in the given text.\n3. Without additional information, it is impossible to accurately describe or compare these cells based solely on the provided passage.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 23.055, "generation_time_seconds": 20.1435, "selection_time_seconds": 2.9037, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 34593, 18037, 323, 5944, 315, 2518, 323, 4158, 6543, 7761, 311, 10542, 862, 11799, 304, 1379, 11, 6083, 11, 323, 729, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.4125, -0.0233, -0.0019, -3.3117, -2.8889, -0.3538, -0.3909, -0.0036, -0.4294, -0.5945, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -1.4888, -0.028, -0.3263, -0.2445, -6.6967, -1.2825, -0.0013, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0053, -0.6978, -0.0094, -0.02