{"id": "739", "question": "what is the difference between sms and mms", "gt": "Sure! Here's my answer based on the given passages:\n\nThe main difference between SMS (Short Message Service) and MMS (Multimedia Messaging Service) is that SMS is limited to sending text-only messages, while MMS allows for sending multimedia content such as images, videos, and audio files, in addition to text.\n\nAccording to passage 1, SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts if they are longer. MMS messages, on the other hand, can carry a larger size of content, including pictures, videos, and audio files, with a maximum size of 300KB.\n\nPassage 2 explains that SMS is a premium service offered by mobile companies, while passage 3 highlights the differences between SMS and MMS, stating that SMS only allows for text, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n\nTherefore, the key differences between SMS and MMS are:\n\n* SMS is limited to text-only messages, while MMS allows for multimedia content.\n* SMS messages are limited to 160 characters and can be split into multiple parts, while MMS messages can carry a larger size of content.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS is a text message service that can only send text messages, while MMS is a multimedia message service that can send multimedia messages such as photos, videos, and audio files. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters, while MMS messages can be up to 2MB in size. SMS messages are typically used for sending short and simple messages, while MMS messages are used for sharing larger and more complex content. In summary, SMS and MMS are two different types of mobile messaging services that have different capabilities and uses.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "The difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS is a text message service that can only send text messages, while MMS is a multimedia message service that can send multimedia messages such as photos, videos, and audio files. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters, while MMS messages can be up to 2MB in size. SMS messages are typically used for sending short and simple messages, while MMS messages are used for sharing larger and more complex content. In summary, SMS and MMS are two different types of mobile messaging services that have different capabilities and uses.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify key features of SMS and MMS mentioned in the passage, such as message type, size, and purpose.\nCompare the features of SMS and MMS to highlight their differences.\nAnalyze the specific examples or numbers provided in the passage to illustrate the differences in message type, size, and purpose between SMS and MMS.\n\nThe difference between SMS and MMS is that SMS is a text message service that can only send text messages, while MMS is a multimedia message service that can send multimedia messages such as photos, videos, and audio files. SMS messages are limited to 160 characters, while MMS messages can be up to 2MB in size. SMS messages are typically used for sending short and simple messages, while MMS messages are used for sharing larger and more complex content. In summary, SMS and MMS are two different types of mobile messaging services that have different capabilities and uses.", "time_sec": 27.951, "generation_time_seconds": 24.3889, "selection_time_seconds": 3.5546, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 5424, 315, 279, 3405, 198, 785, 3405, 17064, 369, 279, 6672, 1948, 29909, 323, 386, 4826, 11, 892, 525, 2176, 4494, 315, 6371, 29522, 3516, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 1516