{"id": "40", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here is a brief answer to the question:\n\nTo get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first, run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic. Then, scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, being careful not to damage the dryer's interior. Next, apply nail polish remover to a clean cloth and rub the plastic to dissolve it. Rinse the area with a damp cloth and then mix liquid laundry soap with water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution and rub the area again. Finally, rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.", "pred": "To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, observe the dryer and locate the lint filter or collecting tray where plastic debris accumulates. Remove this component from the dryer, and check it for any plastic pieces. Use your fingers or a small tool to extract any plastic caught in the filter or tray.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, observe the dryer and locate the lint filter or collecting tray where plastic debris accumulates. Remove this component from the dryer, and check it for any plastic pieces. Use your fingers or a small tool to extract any plastic caught in the filter or tray.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nObserve the dryer and identify the location of the lint filter or collecting tray where plastic debris is typically deposited.\nRemove the lint filter or collecting tray from the dryer.\nCarefully inspect the lint filter or collecting tray for any visible plastic debris. Use your fingers or a small tool to remove any pieces of plastic that are caught in the filter or tray.\n\nAnswer: To remove plastic from a clothes dryer, observe the dryer and locate the lint filter or collecting tray where plastic debris accumulates. Remove this component from the dryer, and check it for any plastic pieces. Use your fingers or a small tool to extract any plastic caught in the filter or tray.", "time_sec": 28.686, "generation_time_seconds": 25.5059, "selection_time_seconds": 3.1671, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 1246, 311, 4057, 12188, 504, 264, 15097, 46622, 13, 2014, 4226, 419, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 2908, 279, 4185, 5413, 369, 17592, 33998, 504, 9058, 388, 13, 45302, 11, 9058, 388, 614, 264, 57920, 4051, 429, 51207, 57920, 323, 33998, 11, 2670, 2613, 12188, 9666, 13, 576, 1156, 3019, 1035, 387, 311, 1779, 323, 4240, 279, 57920, 4051, 311, 5978, 429, 432, 374, 537, 272, 24867, 448, 12188, 476, 1008, 33998, 13, 1416, 279, 57920, 4051, 374, 2480, 11, 4287, 287, 432, 686, 1492, 311, 2797, 279, 46622, 315, 894, 40065, 12188, 382], "logp_list": [-0.9957, -1.3159, -0.0285, -0.3627, -0.0, -0.8028, -0.0, -0.0006, -0.0794, -0.0022, 0.0, -0.0243, -0.407, -0.7258, -0.0176, -0.0075, -0.1265, -0.0271, -0.0098, -0.2782, -0.174, -2.6053, -0.5232, -1.7061, -0.8611, -1.7625, -0.5551, -1.1112, 0.0, -1.8015, -0.359, -0.0, -0.1694, -0.0, -0.004, -0.0487, -0.1782, -1.1537, -0.1083, -1.1615, -0.2776, -0.0194, -4.4517, -2.7802, -0.2617, -0.1029, -4.3926, -0.0838, -0.0798, -0.329, -0.9239, -0.4288, -0.6404, -0.1212, -0.0003, -1.4352, -0.203, -0.0501, -0.508, -0.0019, -0.0001, -1.8622, -1.0342, -1.8888, -0.2529, -0.0188, -0.2698, -0.8309, -0.0001, -0.1643, -0.1483, -0.5893, -0.0046, -0.0089, -0.1554, -1.0307, -0.0389, -0.8794, -0.0001, -0.0052, -0.2789, -0.4343, -1.8838, -0.4307, -0.0198, -1.2026, -0.5723, -2.4461, -2.3553, -0.6173, -0.0111, -0.1399, -0.4875, -0.8931, -0.1557, -1.7671], "cumulative_logprob": -59.4643, "norm_logp": -0.6194, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 96, "avg_logp": -0.6194179058074951}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [4121, 13267, 279, 46622, 323, 10542, 279, 3728, 315, 279, 57920, 4051, 476, 25895, 34688, 1380, 12188, 33998, 374, 111