{"id": "59", "question": "how can i keep birds from building a nest on my porch", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to keep birds from building nests on your porch:\n\n1. Attach bird netting to the eaves around the perimeter of your porch with a staple gun (Passage 1:4). This will prevent birds from reaching the areas they often choose to build their nests.\n2. Install bird netting over the top of the light fixture to block the birds' access to it (Passage 2:1). Choose a non-flammable netting that is safe to use around light bulbs, and ensure that it is installed so that it doesn't entangle birds.\n3. Mount a plastic hawk on or near your porch to scare the birds from the area (Passage 3:1). Move the plastic hawk periodically to avoid the birds becoming accustomed to it.\n\nPlease note that the effectiveness of these methods may vary depending on the type of birds and the location of your porch. If the above methods do not work, you may need to consider other solutions or consult with a professional for assistance.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the specific types of birds that are most likely to build nests on the porch.\nConsider the accessibility of the porch for the birds to reach their building materials.\nConsider the accessibility of the porch for the birds to reach their building materials.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 25.919, "generation_time_seconds": 23.229, "selection_time_seconds": 2.6817, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645,