{"id": "104", "question": "how the body systems work together", "gt": "The body systems work together in order to maintain the normal functioning of the human body. These systems include the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, urinary, endocrine, lymphatic, immune, reproductive, and nervous systems. Each system has its own specific functions, but they also work in conjunction with one another to ensure the overall well-being of the body. For example, the urinary system cleans waste products from various systems such as the skeletal, muscular, digestive, respiratory, circulatory, and nervous systems. Similarly, the respiratory system provides oxygen to all body parts and removes carbon dioxide from the muscular, digestive, skeletal, circulatory, urinary, and nervous systems.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nBased on the given passage, there is not enough information to answer the question \"how the body systems work together.\" The passage does not provide any details about the interaction between body systems or how they collaborate to maintain overall health. Therefore, the logical next step is:\nThe passage does not mention any specific examples, numbers, or comparisons related to how body systems work together. It also does not provide any details about the interaction between body systems or how they collaborate to maintain overall health. Therefore, there is insufficient information to answer the question.\nSince the question \"how the body systems work together\" is not addressed in the given passage and there is no additional context provided, the most logical step is to conclude that the required information is not available within the given text.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 27.738, "generation_ti