{"id": "133", "question": "how to roast individual garlic cloves", "gt": "To roast individual garlic cloves, preheat your oven to 400°F (205°C). Peel and discard the papery outer layers of the garlic bulb, leaving the skins of the cloves intact. Cut 1/4 to 1/2 inch from the top of the cloves to expose them. Place the garlic heads in a baking pan, cut side up, and drizzle a couple teaspoons of olive oil over each exposed head, rubbing it over the cloves. Roast the cloves in the preheated oven for about 45 minutes to an hour, or until they are softened. Store the roasted garlic cloves in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 10 days.", "pred": "The method for roasting individual garlic cloves involves roasting them in an oven. The tools needed for this method are a baking sheet and an oven. Garlic cloves do not need to be peeled before roasting. To roast the garlic cloves, place them on a baking sheet in a single layer and roast them in the oven at 425°F (220°C) for 20-25 minutes. The cloves should be checked for doneness by checking the color and texture.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "The method for roasting individual garlic cloves involves roasting them in an oven. The tools needed for this method are a baking sheet and an oven. Garlic cloves do not need to be peeled before roasting. To roast the garlic cloves, place them on a baking sheet in a single layer and roast them in the oven at 425°F (220°C) for 20-25 minutes. The cloves should be checked for doneness by checking the color and texture.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n- Identify the method: Determine if the method involves roasting in an oven or on a stovetop.\n- Identify the tools: Determine the tools needed for the method, such as a baking sheet, oven, or skillet.\n- Identify the preparation: Determine if the garlic cloves need to be peeled before roasting, and if so, how they should be peeled.\n\nThe method for roasting individual garlic cloves involves roasting them in an oven. The tools needed for this method are a baking sheet and an oven. Garlic cloves do not need to be peeled before roasting. To roast the garlic cloves, place them on a baking sheet in a single layer and roast them in the oven at 425°F (220°C) for 20-25 minutes. The cloves should be checked for doneness by checking the color and texture.", "time_sec": 22.359, "generation_time_seconds": 19.493, "selection_time_seconds": 2.8589, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2661, 21085, 1558, 537, 3410, 894, 1995, 389, 1246, 311, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.201, -1.2561, -0.0565, -0.0156, -0.0, -0.1206, -0.9597, -0.3179, -0.4458, -0.0045, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0002, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0032, -0.238, -32.6042, -28.5417, -18.3095, -21.043, -16.6725, -11.6361, -10.1175], "cumulative_logprob": -143.5437, "norm_logp": -5.981, "input_len": 139, "output_tokens": 24, "avg_logp": -5.980979919433594}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [1249, 57685, 3842, 30635, 84288, 11, 498, 646, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.6594, -0.3551, -0.0003, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0034, -1.3752, -1.3025, -0.0517, -0.0091, -0.0147, -0.101, -Infinity, -31.6667, -21.4587, -20.4292, -21.355, -13.3436, -10.8806, -11.4897, -10.505, -9.3948, -8.7194, -9.1832], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_len": 139, "output_tokens": 24, "avg_logp": -Infinity}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 2, "token_ids": [12, 64547, 279, 1714, 25, 29901, 421, 279, 1714, 17601, 926, 14725, 304, 458, 23387, 476, 389, 264, 357, 859, 295, 453, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-5.8885, -0.2955, -0.0082, -1.1822, -3.1378, -1.2589, -0.7788, -0.0108, -2.8386, -0.1437, -0.5251, 0.0, -1.5363, -0.2772, -0.0, -1.0538, -0.35, 