{"id": "142", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is as follows:\n\nThe scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded, as per Section 43(6) of the Income Tax Act. The block concept applies to all assets falling within the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation, and any alterations to the value of the block must be made in accordance with the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act. The assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of the discarded asset (i.e., opening WDV of such asset less scrap value) even if the asset is not used for business or professional purposes in that year or subsequent years.\n\nTherefore, the treatment for an asset that is discarded as per the Income Tax Act is to reduce the scrap value from the block in the previous year and claim depreciation on the residual value.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the specific provisions or sections of the Income Tax Act that address the treatment of assets when they are discarded. Look for any explicit mention of disposal, sale, or abandonment of assets and how these actions affect the income tax liability of the individual or entity involved.\nIdentify the specific provisions or sections of the Income Tax Act that address the treatment of assets when they are discarded. Look for any explicit mention of disposal, sale, or abandonment of assets and how these actions affect the income tax liability of the individual or entity involved.\nLook for specific sections or clauses in the Income Tax Act that detail the treatment of assets when they are discarded, focusing on how this impacts tax liabilities.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 25.882, "generation_time_seconds": 22.7081, "selection_time_seconds": 3.1649, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2661, 21085, 1558, 537, 3410, 1995, 911, 279, 6380, 315, 458, 9329, 43210, 4092, 311, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.7783, -1.3082, -0.8629, -0.0273, -0.0, -0.1502, -0.8682, -0.325, -0.0026, -0.0059, -0.1206, -0.9244, -0.0, -2.2127, -2.1799, -0.0, -0.0072, -0.1429, -0.0, -0.0, -0.003, -0.479, -31.875, -26.0417, -17.4108, -15.0044, -11.8769, -11.3289, -10.053, -8.9825, -8.1693, -7.4388, -6.5598, -5.7969, -5.2486, -5.5424, -5.5107, -5.6411, -5.2876, -5.5346, -5.3604, -4.7929, -5.6089, -6.9405, -6.6622, -7.0187, -6.8666, -6.4347, -6.2595, -6.1181, -6.6333, -7.121, -6.7538, -5.933, -6.371, -6.9223, -6.7619, -6.6256, -6.5652, -5.0189, -4.7803, -5.7505, -5.9534, -5.95, -5.8268, -5.1941, -5.5488, -5.7286, -6.5131, -6.4981, -7.5319, -5.8702, -4.8558, -4.4253, -4.4253], "cumulative_logprob": -415.322, "norm_logp": -5.5376, "input_len": 146, "output_tokens": 75, "avg_logp": -5.537621974945068}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 369, 279, 6380, 315, 458, 9329, 979, 432, 374, 43210, 4092, 311, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 13, 576, 3897, 21085, 1558, 537, 6644, 894, 3151, 1995, 911, 279, 6380, 315, 458, 9329, 979, 432, 374, 43210, 13, 15277, 11, 1052, 374, 537, 3322, 1995, 311, 4226, 279, 3405, 3118, 389, 279, 2661, 4676