{"id": "259", "question": "how to clean dryer vent", "gt": "Sure, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean dryer vent\" based on the given passages:\n\nTo clean the dryer vent, start by locating the vent cover on the outside of the house and removing it. Then, remove the vent from the back of the dryer and use a dryer vent brush to clean the lint from the vent and the hole in the back of the dryer. Reconnect the vent and move the dryer back against the wall. Additionally, consider removing the bottom front panel of the dryer and cleaning the area around the lint filter for a more thorough cleaning. Use a vacuum nozzle to clean the lint deposits and ensure your dryer runs efficiently.\n\nIf the passages did not contain the necessary information to answer the question, I would have replied with \"Unable to answer based on given passages.\"", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of dryer and its specific vent configuration.\nExamine the dryer's manufacturer recommendations for cleaning the vent.\nCheck if there are any built-in cleaning features or instructions in the dryer's manual.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 22.075, "generation_time_seconds": 19.3559, "selection_time_seconds": 2.7105, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 4185, 5413, 369, 15826, 46622, 80207, 624, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 1759, 279, 7375, 323, 7236, 11136, 1483, 369, 419, 3383, 624, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 81917, 279, 12650, 315, 15826, 279, 46622, 10378, 624, 8304, 220, 19, 25, 60785, 1246, 311, 4057, 279, 46622, 10378, 323, 2615, 279, 10378, 13647, 624, 8304, 220, 20, 25, 60785, 279, 1882, 315, 15826, 279, 10378, 13647, 323, 46622, 10378, 624, 8304, 220