{"id": "300", "question": "how to make hot water heater circulate", "gt": "To make a hot water heater circulate, one can install a recirculation system. The system consists of a pump that pulls hot water from the water heater and simultaneously sends cool water from the hot water lines back to the water heater to be reheated and reused. This ensures that hot water is always available without having to wait for it to circulate naturally. Recirculation systems can be controlled by a button, timer, or motion sensor.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe question asks how to make a hot water heater circulate. To address this, we need information about hot water heaters and their circulation mechanisms. The passages provided do not contain this information, so we cannot determine a method for circulation.\nThe passages do not provide specific details about hot water heaters or their circulation mechanisms. Therefore, there is insufficient information to determine how to make a hot water heater circulate.\nThe passages do not provide any information about hot water heaters or their circulation mechanisms.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 23.886, "generation_time_seconds": 21.1107, "selection_time_seconds": 2.7674, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2661, 3491, 374, 25, 330, 5158, 311, 1281, 4017, 3015, 42238, 4225, 6334, 1837, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 1516