{"id": "320", "question": "what is the effect of carbon footprint", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it is clear that the effect of a carbon footprint is a measure of the negative impact of human activities on the environment. The measurement of a carbon footprint typically indicates the amount of carbon dioxide and other greenhouse gases produced through daily activities. Additionally, reducing one's carbon footprint can have a positive impact on the environment, even if the changes may seem small.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the key components of a carbon footprint.\nIdentify the effects of a carbon footprint on the environment.\nExamine the specific examples or comparisons given in the passages to understand the impact of carbon footprint on the environment.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 19.352, "generation_time_seconds": 16.7501, "selection_time_seconds": 2.5948, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 32711, 7354, 1373, 41018, 279, 6961, 3565, 315, 279, 3491, 311, 8253, 279, 6239, 315, 12499, 42872, 13, 16246, 279, 3405, 11, 279, 1790, 19819, 3019, 1035, 387, 311, 20961, 279, 3897, 46769, 369, 1995, 911, 12499, 42872, 323, 1181, 6239, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.6512, -0.9888, -0.0537, -6.2272, -0.6127, -0.0087, -0.1388, -0.0007, -1.8722, -0.0153, -0.9421, -1.3228, -0.2533, -0.0364, -4.1716, -0.0, -0.2667, -0.0003, -0.0452, -3.836, -0.2165, -1.0518, -0.3943, -0.4173, -0.5316, -0.0083, -0.0125, -0.7166, -0.0155, -0.0034, -3.4214, -0.2007, -1.1641, -0.0109, -0.2661, -0.6326, -1.0003, -0.1995, -0.1427, -0.0303, -0.0002, -0.01, -0.0685, -0.5158], "cumulative_logprob": -32.4746, "norm_logp": -0.7381, "input_len": 140, "output_tokens": 44, "avg_l