us": "success"}}
{"id": "42", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some ways to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic, then scrape it off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper. (Passage 1)\n2. Heat the plastic with a hair dryer or heat gun to make it easier to peel off. Once heated, use a cloth to peel off the plastic. (Passage 2)\n3. Soak a cloth in an acetone-based nail polish remover and use it to scrub the remaining plastic off of the element after leaving it on the element for 5 minutes. Then, wipe the coils with a clean, damp cloth and remove any remaining residue with a cloth dipped in a solution of warm water and dish soap. (Passage 3)\n\nUnable to answer based on the given passages. The passages do not provide specific instructions on how to remove plastic from the drum of a clothes dryer.", "pred": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first determine the type of plastic that is stuck in the dryer. Then, carefully remove the plastic from the dryer, being careful not to damage the dryer or the plastic itself.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first determine the type of plastic that is stuck in the dryer. Then, carefully remove the plastic from the dryer, being careful not to damage the dryer or the plastic itself.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe steps you have provided are instructions on how to get plastic out of a clothes dryer. The steps include:\nThe first step is to determine the type of plastic that is stuck in the dryer.\nThe second step is to carefully remove the plastic from the dryer, avoiding damaging the dryer or the plastic itself.\n\nAnswer: To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first determine the type of plastic that is stuck in the dryer. Then, carefully remove the p