{"id": "114", "question": "how are water shares transferred", "gt": "Water shares are transferred by following a set of steps. The seller must return the Water Stock Certificate and sign the back of the certificate. The new owner of the property must provide proof of ownership. A fee of $75.00 must be paid to process the transfer. After completing these steps, a new Water Stock Certificate will be issued to the new owner of record.", "pred": "Water shares are typically transferred through a legal process that involves the filing of a document with the appropriate governmental authority, such as a water district or a state agency. This document, known as a water share transfer affidavit or similar, must include specific information such as the names of the transferring and receiving parties, the type and quantity of the water share being transferred, and any other relevant details. The transfer is subject to the approval of the governing body overseeing the water resources, which may require a public notice and an opportunity for objections. Once approved, the transfer becomes effective, and the water share is legally transferred from the transferring party to the receiving party.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Water shares are typically transferred through a legal process that involves the filing of a document with the appropriate governmental authority, such as a water district or a state agency. This document, known as a water share transfer affidavit or similar, must include specific information such as the names of the transferring and receiving parties, the type and quantity of the water share being transferred, and any other relevant details. The transfer is subject to the approval of the governing body overseeing the water resources, which may require a public notice and an opportunity for objections. Once approved, the transfer becomes effective, and the water share is legally transferred from the transferring party to the receiving party.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\nExplain the process of transferring water shares, including any legal or administrative procedures involved.\nIdentify the specific types of water shares that can be transferred, such as irrigation shares or domestic shares.\n\nAnswer: Water shares are typically transferred through a legal process that involves the filing of a document with the appropriate governmental authority, such as a water district or a state agency. This document, known as a water share transfer affidavit or similar, must include specific information such as the names of the transferring and receiving parties, the type and quantity of the water share being transferred, and any other relevant details. The transfer is subject to the approval of the governing body overseeing the water resources, which may require a public notice and an opportunity for objections. Once approved, the transfer becomes effective, and the water share is legally transferred from the transferring party to the receiving party.", "time_sec": 27.339, "generation_time_seconds": 24.0397, "selection_time_seconds": 3.2927, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 11, 330, 5158, 525, 3015, 13248, 22409, 1189, 1096, 7460, 8660, 279, 1882, 315, 49951, 15278, 476, 10431, 3188, 315, 3015, 13248, 13, 576, 2661, 21085, 1558, 537, 3410, 894, 3151, 1995, 389, 1246, 3015, 13248, 525, 22409, 13, 15277, 11, 279, 4226, 374, 25, 41444, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.8582, -1.4574, -0.0235, -5.1316, -0.0011, -1.1944, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.7481, -3.8092, -0.8516, -1.305, -0.0021, -0.0941, -1.1232, -0.0174, -2.7735, -0.0053, -0.5992, -0.0154, -0.1402, -0.0016, -0.0023, -0.2267, -0.6694, -1.3755, -0.0098, -0.028, -0.0, -0.0538, -1.8227, -0.3851, -0.3154, -2.9921, -0.4966, -0.0541, -0.0, -0.0, -0