{"id": "124", "question": "building a lean-to shed", "gt": "To build a lean-to shed, start by preparing the site with a 4\" layer of compacted gravel. Cut two 4 x 4 skids to a length of 70 2/4\" and set and level them according to the shed building plans. Cut two 2 x 6 rim joists at 7 3/4\" and six joists at 44 3/4\". Assemble the floor and place it on the skids as indicated in the floor framing section of the plans. Check for squareness and anchor the frame to the skids with four joist clip angles. Cut two more 4 x 4s to a length of 6 feet for the skids and, when the frame is square, toenail the floor joists to the skids. Attach 3/4-inch tongue-and-groove plywood flooring onto the frame. The walls for the shed are constructed separately and then raised onto the frame. The size of the shed can be adjusted as needed.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nBuilding a lean-to shed involves several key steps and considerations to ensure a successful and sturdy structure. The first logical reasoning step is to assess the available space and determine the dimensions of the shed. This involves measuring the length, width, and height of the area where the shed will be built. For example, if the space available is 10 feet by 8 feet, the shed could be designed to fit these dimensions, allowing for a 10-foot length and an 8-foot width. This step is crucial as it sets the foundation for the entire construction process and ensures that the shed will fit within the designated area without causing any\nAfter assessing the available space and determining the dimensions, the next logical step in building a lean-to shed is to plan the layout and materials needed. This involves selecting the appropriate materials such as wood, nails, and any other hardware required. For instance, choosing pressure-treated lumber for the exterior and interior walls, and ensuring a sufficient amount of nails for securing the structure is essential. Additionally, planning the placement of doors and windows, if any, is crucial to ensure the shed functions effectively and fits the intended purpose. This step also includes considering the type of roof needed, whether it will be a simple gable roof or a more complex design,\nNext logical reasoning step: Prepare the construction site. This involves clearing the area of any debris, leveling the ground, and setting up any necessary tools and materials. Ensuring the ground is level and free of obstacles will make the construction process smoother and safer. Setting up tools and materials in an organized manner will also help streamline the construction process, allowing for efficient use of resources and time.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 37.883, "generation_time_seconds": 34.3826, "selection_time_seconds": 3.488, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 7236, 4362, 369, 4752, 264, 15651, 4686, 24354, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 