{"id": "144", "question": "how to sew a zipper gusset", "gt": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "pred": "A zipper gusset is a piece of fabric that is sewn into the bottom of a bag or other item to allow for more room when opening and closing with a zipper. Its purpose is to prevent the fabric from becoming too tight when the item is fully opened.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: A zipper gusset is a piece of fabric that is sewn into the bottom of a bag or other item to allow for more room when opening and closing with a zipper. Its purpose is to prevent the fabric from becoming too tight when the item is fully opened.\n\nThe materials needed for sewing a zipper gusset include fabric, a zipper, sewing thread, a needle, and a sewing machine.\n\nThe sewing process for creating a zipper gusset involves the following steps:\n\n1. Cut a piece of fabric to the desired size for the gusset. This should be slightly larger than the area where the gusset will be sewn into the item.\n\n2. Fold the fabric in half lengthwise and mark the center line with a chalk or fabric marker.\n\n3. Place the zipper on the fabric with the teeth facing upward and the slider positioned on the center line. Pin the zipper in place to hold it in position.\n\n4. Use the sewing machine to stitch the zipper to the fabric, starting at the top and working down. Be sure to backstitch at the beginning and end of the stitching to secure the zipper in place.\n\n5. Remove the pins and finish sewing the zipper to the fabric.\n\n6. Turn the fabric right side out and press the seam flat with an iron.\n\n7. Fold the fabric under at the top and bottom to create a neat edge. Pin the fold in place.\n\n8. Use the sewing machine to stitch the fold in place, starting at the bottom and working up. Be sure to backstitch at the beginning and end of the stitching to secure the fold in place.\n\n9. Turn the fabric right side out and press the seam flat with an iron.\n\n10. Fold the fabric under at the top and bottom to create a neat edge. Pin the fold in place.\n\n11. Use the sewing machine to stitch the fold in place, starting at the bottom and working up. Be sure to backstitch at the beginning and end of the stitching to secure the fold in place.\n\n12. Turn the fabric right side out and press the seam flat with an iron.\n\n13. Fold the fabric under at the top and bottom to create a neat edge. Pin the fold in place.\n\n14. Use the sewing machine to stitch the fold in place, starting at the bottom and working up. Be sure to backstitch at the beginning and end of the stitching to secure the fold in place.\n\n15. Turn the fabric right side out and press the seam flat", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExplain what a zipper gusset is and its purpose.\nExplain the materials needed for sewing a zipper gusset.\nExplain the sewing process for creating a zipper gusset, including the steps involved.\n\nAnswer: A zipper gusset is a piece of fabric that is sewn into the bottom of a bag or other item to allow for more room when opening and closing with a zipper. Its purpose is to prevent the fabric from becoming too tight when the item is fully opened.\n\nThe materials needed for sewing a zipper gusset include fabric, a zipper, sewing thread, a needle, and a sewing machine.\n\nThe sewing process for creating a zipper gusset involves the following steps:\n\n1. Cut a piece of fabric to the desired size for the gusset. This should be slightly larger than the area where the gusset will be sewn into the item.\n\n2. Fold the fabric in half lengthwise and mark the center line with a chalk or fabric marker.\n\n3. Place the zipper on the fabric with the teeth facing upward and the slider positioned on the center line. Pin the zipper in place to hold it in position.\n\n4. Use the sewing machine to stitch the zipper to the fabric, starting at the top and working down. Be sure to backstitch at the beginning and end of the stitching to secure the zipper in place.\n\n5. Remove the pins and finish sewing the zipper to the fabric.\n\n6. Turn the fabric right side out and press the seam flat with an iron.\n\n7. Fold the fabric under at the top and bottom to create a neat edge. Pin the fold in place.\n\n8. Use the sewing machine to stitch the fold in place, starting at the bottom and working up. Be sure to backstitch at the beginning and end of the stitching to secure the fold in place.\n\n9. Turn the fabric right side out and press the seam flat with an iron.\n\n10. Fold the fabric under at the top and bottom to create a neat edge. Pin the fold in place.\n\n11. Use the sewing machine to stitch the fold in place, starting at the bottom and working up. Be sure to backstitch at the beginning and end of the stitching to secure the fold in place.\n\n12. Turn the fabric right side out and press the seam flat with an iron.\n\n13. Fold the fabric under at the top and bottom to create a neat edge. Pin the fold in place.\n\n14. Use the sewing machine to stitch the fold in place, starting at the bottom and working up. Be sure to backstitch at the beginning and end of the stitching to secure the fold in place.\n\n15. Turn the fabric right side out and press the seam flat", "time_sec": 52.66, "generation_time_seconds": 49.2773, "selection_time_seconds": 3.3741, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 32711, 7354, 525, 510, 16, 13, 64547, 279, 7428, 315, 279, 68761, 342, 355, 746, 624, 17, 13, 48995, 5871, 7236, 323, 7375, 624, 18, 13, 31166, 279, 13055, 369, 51219, 624, 19, 13, 48384, 279, 68761, 311, 279, 13055, 624, 20, 13, 49213, 279, 342, 355, 746, 1119, 279, 13055, 624, 21, 13, 35533, 279, 12822, 369, 264, 28485, 11094, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3035, -0.9444, -0.0236, -0.0342, -1.3481, -0.0049, -0.0001, -0.3174, -0.0038, -2.0607, -0.0744, -1.5205, -0.4539, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.3514, -0.0011, 0.0, -0.5757, -0.437