{"id": "169", "question": "show me how can i make gragh for my research", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to create a bar graph for your research:\n\n1. Collect your data: The first step is to gather all the data you want to represent in your graph. Make sure the data is organized and easy to compare.\n2. Decide on the x-axis and y-axis: The x-axis typically represents the category or group being compared, while the y-axis represents the value or amount of each category.\n3. Determine the height of the graph: The height of the graph will depend on the highest value in your data set. Make sure to choose a height that allows for clear representation of all the data points.\n4. Create the bars: Use rectangular bars to represent each category, making sure the height of each bar is proportional to the value it represents.\n5. Add labels and titles: Label each bar with its corresponding category and add a title to the graph that describes the data being represented.\n6. Consider using a pie chart: If you have only a few data points to display and each one is substantially different in scale, a pie chart might be a better option.\n7. Format and refine: Make sure the graph is visually appealing and easy to read. Adjust the scaling of the y-axis if needed, and consider adding colors or shading to make the graph more engaging.\n\nBy following these steps, you should be able to create a clear and effective bar graph for your research. Good luck!", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe given question asks how to make a graph for research. To analyze the reasoning step by step, we need to consider the following:\nStep 1: Identify the type of research data\nStep 2: Choose the appropriate type of graph\nStep 3: Gather the necessary data\nStep 4: Select a graphing tool or software\nStep 5: Input the data into the graphing tool\nStep 6: Customize the graph to meet research requirements\nStep 7: Review and finalize the graph\nStep 8: Document the graph in your research\nStep 9: Present the graph in your research (e.g., in a report, presentation, or publication) with proper labeling and annotations.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 42.547, "generation_time_seconds": 39.3825, "selection_time_seconds": 3.1539, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [16250, 2685, 279, 7428, 323, 6891, 315, 697, 3412, 13, 64547, 279, 1376, 821, 3501, 323, 7332, 429, 498, 1366, 311, 50087, 304, 697, 4771, 13, 29901, 279, 943, 315, 4771, 429, 1850, 10868, 697, 821, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 1555, 4771, 11, 3619, 9487, 11, 30281, 11, 44477, 7089, 11, 4992, 35334, 20513, 476, 10549, 279, 821, 369, 279, 4771, 13, 22201, 264, 4771, 287, 5392, 476, 3162, 320, 68, 1302, 2572, 5100, 21029, 11, 5085, 60472, 11, 49347, 11, 13027, 43902, 20186, 1741, 438, 6867, 15406, 476, 1345, 370, 1512, 568, 5443, 279, 3162, 311, 1855, 279, 4771, 11, 42368, 279, 24745, 11, 9201, 11, 323, 36566, 438, 4362, 311, 13444, 19032, 697, 3412, 14613, 13, 3393, 279, 4771, 369, 31273, 323, 91494, 11, 323, 1281], "logp_list": [-4.3912, -0.0084, -0.0442, -0.8407, -0.4288, -0.399, -0.0, -1.5019, -0.0083, -0.8429, -2.0566, -0.0068, -0.1414, -1.3492, -0.42, -0.3445, -0.1063, -0.6118, -0.6706, -0.171, -0.0, -0.5542, -2.4284, -0.0352, -0.0028, -0.0182, -0.9111, -0.0075, -0.081, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.006, -0.0074, -0.5083, -0.0799, -0.0013, -0.5133, -0.0011, -0.0, -0.0002, -0.0981, -0.0021, -0.043, -0.0003, -0.5944, -0.0, -0.9781, -0.0987, -0.105, -0.0007, -0.6208, -0.1431, -0.0137, -1.1614, -1.7704, -1.1168, -0.9236, -0.0113, -1.0527, -0.7268, -0.0009, -0.0418, -0.8339, -0.0793, -0.4911, -0.0019, -0.0789, -0.0041, -0.0, -1.0781, -0.0038, -0.