{"id": "197", "question": "leasing meaning", "gt": "Leasing refers to a process in which a firm obtains the use of fixed assets by making contractual, periodic, and tax-deductible payments to the owner of those assets. The lessee is the party receiving the services or assets under the lease contract, while the lessor is the owner of the assets.", "pred": "Based on the passage, leasing refers to the practice of renting property or equipment for a specific period of time, often with the option to purchase the property or equipment at the end of the lease. The passage does not provide a detailed definition, but it implies that leasing involves a long-term rental agreement with a possibility of ownership at the end of the lease term.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Based on the passage, leasing refers to the practice of renting property or equipment for a specific period of time, often with the option to purchase the property or equipment at the end of the lease. The passage does not provide a detailed definition, but it implies that leasing involves a long-term rental agreement with a possibility of ownership at the end of the lease term.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\n- Identify the key concept: The question asks for the meaning of \"leasing.\"\n- Locate relevant information: Look for definitions or explanations of what leasing means in the given passages.\nAnalyze the passages for any direct definitions or explanations of leasing.\n\nBased on the passage, leasing refers to the practice of renting property or equipment for a specific period of time, often with the option to purchase the property or equipment at the end of the lease. The passage does not provide a detailed definition, but it implies that leasing involves a long-term rental agreement with a possibility of ownership at the end of the lease term.", "time_sec": 22.6, "generation_time_seconds": 19.8642, "selection_time_