0001, -0.0162, -0.19, -1.3749, -0.7377, -0.5205, -0.0, -0.0165, -0.1546, -0.7707, -0.2541, -0.5648, -0.1117, -0.0297, -0.5152, -0.0082, -0.0006, -0.5394, -0.275, -2.8013, -0.0, -0.7557, -0.6968, -0.9824, -3.8007, -1.3212, -0.0293, -1.5491, -4.0352, -0.0074, -0.0388, -1.0471, -0.0006, -0.1075, -0.2083, -0.5353, -0.1256], "cumulative_logprob": -42.4172, "norm_logp": -0.5811, "input_len": 167, "output_tokens": 73, "judge_p": 0.05, "selected": true}, "eval_metrics": {"Token-F1": 9.84, "GAVIE-Rel": 5.0, "GAVIE-Acc": 3.0, "Status": "success"}}
{"id": "210", "question": "differences between elements compounds and mixtures", "gt": "Elements are the purest form of a chemical substance and are composed of only one type of atom, meaning all the atoms in an element have the same number of protons. Compounds, on the other hand, are substances composed of two or more different elements and are also pure substances. Mixtures are physical combinations of elements or compounds where the parts of the mixture are not chemically bonded and so retain their own identity. The individual components of a mixture can be physically separated from each other. Mixtures have variable compositions and show the properties of their constituent substances. Elements and compounds just mix together to form a mixture and no new compound is formed.", "pred": "Elements are pure substances consisting of only one type of atom. Examples include hydrogen (H), oxygen (O), and gold (Au). Compounds are pure substances consisting of two or more different types of atoms chemically bonded together in a fixed ratio. For example, water (H2O) is a compound made of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom. Mixtures are combinations of two or more substances where the components retain their individual properties and are not chemically bonded. For instance, saltwater is a mixture of salt and water, where the salt and water can be separated by physical means. The key difference is that elements and compounds are pure substances with specific compositions, while mixtures are blends of substances that can be separated without chemical changes.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Elements are pure substances consisting of only one type of atom. Examples include hydrogen (H), oxygen (O), and gold (Au). Compounds are pure substances consisting of two or more different types of atoms chemically bonded together in a fixed ratio. For example, water (H2O) is a compound made of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom. Mixtures are combinations of two or more substances where the components retain their individual properties and are not chemically bonded. For instance, saltwater is a mixture of salt and water, where the salt and water can be separated by physical means. The key difference is that elements and compounds are pure substances with specific compositions, while mixtures are blends of substances that can be separated without chemical changes.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the essential characteristics of elements, compounds, and mixtures based on the information provided.\nAnalyze the given passages to extract specific examples, numbers, or comparisons that describe the differences between elements, compounds, and mixtures.\nSummarize the key distinctions between elements, compounds, and mixtures based on the analysis of the given passages.\n\nElements are pure substances consisting of only one type of atom. Examples include hydrogen (H), oxygen (O), and gold (Au). Compounds are pure substances consisting of two or more different types of atoms chemically bonded together in a fixed ratio. For example, water (H2O) is a compound made of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom. Mixtures are combinations of two or more substances where the components retain their individual properties and are not chemically bonded. For instance, saltwater is a mixture of salt and water, where the salt and water can be separated by physical means. The key difference is that elements and compounds are pure substances with specific compositions, while mixtures are blends of substances that can be separated without chemical changes.", "time_sec": 31.863, "generation_time_seconds": 28.897, "selection_time_seconds": 2.9557, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 1376, 17452, 315, 5424, 11, 31146, 11, 323, 6514, 18513, 3118, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 46769, 13, 151645, 