{"id": "223", "question": "how to fix lift valve in toilet", "gt": "Based on the given passages, to fix a lift valve in a toilet, you should follow these steps:\n1. Shut off the water supply valve to the toilet.\n2. Remove the old flapper valve by slipping it off the mounting arms and remove the broken lift chain.\n3. Install a new flapper valve and chain.\n4. Adjust the lift chain by moving the metal clip up or down a couple of links.\n5. Cut off any excess lift chain to prevent tangling.\n6. Push the solid end of the toilet lift arm into the flush handle and secure it tightly.\n7. Connect the chain to the third hole on the lift arm closest to the edge.\n8. Use pliers to securely fasten the chain.\n9. Turn the water valve back on.\n10. Test the flush of the toilet and adjust the chain if needed.\n\nNote: The given passages provide step-by-step instructions for fixing a lift valve in a toilet.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the specific type of lift valve in the toilet. Common types include gravity-flush and pressure-assisted flush lift valves.\nIdentify the specific brand and model of the lift valve in the toilet. Different brands and models may have unique features and require specific repair techniques.\nAccess the lift valve by removing the toilet seat and tank lid. Identify the type and model of the lift valve for specific repair instructions.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 18.66, "generation_time_seconds": 15.6381, "selection_time_seconds": 3.013, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [4418, 279, 2661, 21085, 26364, 311, 10542, 279, 1995, 5435, 311, 35251, 264, 11893, 31430, 304, 264, 26214, 13, 9192, 369, 894, 3151, 7354, 11, 7375, 11, 476, 5413, 9733