{"id": "249", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "To grill pork chops according to allrecipes.com, start by preheating an outdoor grill for medium heat and lightly oil the grate. In a bowl, mix together the seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse the pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. With your hands, massage the spice rub into the meat and allow to stand for 10 minutes. Finally, grill the chops over indirect heat until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the key components of the question: The question asks for information on how to grill pork chops, specifically from Allrecipes.com. This indicates that the answer should be a step-by-step guide or instructions for grilling pork chops as provided by Allrecipes.com.\nRetrieve the information: Look for a section on Allrecipes.com that provides instructions for grilling pork chops. This information will likely be in a recipe or article format.\nLocate and extract the instructions: Once the relevant section is found, carefully read and extract the instructions for grilling pork chops. This may include details on the ingredients needed, preparation steps, cooking times, and any specific techniques or tips provided by Allrecipes.com.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 20.301, "generation_time_seconds": 17.3099, "selection_time_seconds": 2.9825, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 