{"id": "278", "question": "what is severe osteoporosis", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, severe osteoporosis refers to a condition where the bones have been significantly weakened to the point of causing symptoms such as back pain, loss of height, and fractures. According to passage 3, osteoporosis typically has no symptoms until significant bone damage has occurred, making it a \"silent disease\" until it reaches this advanced stage. Passage 2 also highlights that compression fractures of the spine are a common cause of osteoporosis pain, which can be severe and debilitating. Therefore, severe osteoporosis is characterized by a high risk of fractures, particularly in the spine and hips, as well as persistent back pain and loss of height.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 19.706, "generation_time_seconds": 16.8752, "selection_time_seconds": 2.8221, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [5501, 3410, 279, 1790, 19819, 32711, 3019, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-4.2474, -0.0251, -0.0074, -0.7874, -0.0133, -0.0085, -0.0004, -0.4273, -0.0015, -27.7083, -21.875, -9.1697, -7.7518, -7.7171, -6.1338, -4.4022, -5.611, -6.8058, -7.152, -6.7042, -6.1118, -5.7661, -3.1733, -2.7738, -2.6441, -2.6175, -3.5026, -5.2787, -6.1181, -5.9792, -5.2598, -4.8927, -4.6699, -5.0228, -5.509, -5.7567], "cumulative_logprob": -