{"id": "337", "question": "how to get rid of ticks from dogs", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's how to get rid of ticks from dogs:\n\n1. Check your dog's body thoroughly, especially in areas like inside and behind the ears, around the eyes, and other favorite tick hiding places.\n2. Use a pair of tweezers to grasp the head of the tick where it attaches to the skin, and wear gloves if needed.\n3. Pull on the tick gently and steadily, making sure not to yank it away from your dog too quickly.\n4. Regularly use tick control products on your dog, as recommended by your veterinarian, to prevent ticks from attaching to your dog in the first place.\n\nIf you have any further questions or concerns, consult your veterinarian for advice.", "pred": "The passage does not provide information on how to get rid of ticks from dogs.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "The passage does not provide information on how to get rid of ticks from dogs.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the symptoms of tick infestation in dogs\nIdentify the common locations where ticks attach to dogs\nIdentify the methods to remove ticks physically from dogs\n\nThe passage does not provide information on how to get rid of ticks from dogs.", "time_sec": 34.96, "generation_time_seconds": 31.9668, "selection_time_seconds": 2.9834, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 5413, 2500, 369, 17592, 29957, 504, 12590, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3595, -0.0024, -0.2828, -1.6609, -5.8489, -0.0939, -0.1277, -0.0005, -0.0025, -0.0046, -