{"id": "381", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, first click on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings. Then, switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group. Click on the Sort option. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu to select a column by name. The names correspond to the headings typed in the first row of your data. Alternatively, you can use Kutools for Excel's Sort Sheets tool to sort all worksheets.", "pred": "Select the data you want to sort, choose the appropriate sorting option in Excel (such as \"Sort A to Z\" or \"Sort Z to A\"), and then apply the selected sorting option to the data to rearrange the rows based on the specified alphabetical order.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Select the data you want to sort, choose the appropriate sorting option in Excel (such as \"Sort A to Z\" or \"Sort Z to A\"), and then apply the selected sorting option to the data to rearrange the rows based on the specified alphabetical order.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe first step in arranging an Excel sheet alphabetically is to select the data you want to sort.\nThe next logical reasoning step is to choose the appropriate sorting option in Excel, which typically involves selecting the \"Sort A to Z\" or \"Sort Z to A\" option depending on the desired order.\nThe next logical reasoning step is to apply the selected sorting option to the data, which will rearrange the rows in the Excel sheet based on the specified alphabetical order.\n\nAnswer: Select the data you want to sort, choose the appropriate sorting option in Excel (such as \"Sort A to Z\" or \"Sort Z to A\"), and then apply the selected sorting option to the data to rearrange the rows based on the specified alphabetical order.", "time_sec": 28.475, "generation_time_seco