{"id": "431", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first determine the extent of the tarnish. If the jewelry is slightly dull, filmy, or starting to discolor, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth into the solution. Rub the jewelry with the cloth, rinse in cool water, and buff with a cloth until dry. If the tarnish is heavier, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water. Wet the jewelry and apply the cleaner with a soft, lint-free cloth. If your silver jewelry is lightly tarnished, you can also try submerging it in a hot saltwater bath. Ensure that if your jewelry has gemstones, they won't be affected by the saltwater. For diamonds, clean with warm soapy water and a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush, and pat dry with a soft cloth.", "pred": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the type of jewelry: Determine if the jewelry is made of gold, silver, or another material that can tarnish.\n\n2. Choose the appropriate cleaning solution:\n   - For silver: Use a mixture of baking soda and water. Mix one part baking soda with two parts water to create a paste. Apply the paste to the tarnished areas and let it sit for 15-20 minutes.\n   - For gold: Use a mixture of lemon juice and water. Mix equal parts of lemon juice and water in a small bowl. Apply the mixture to the tarnished areas and rub gently with a soft cloth or brush. Rinse with warm water and dry.\n\n3. Polish the jewelry: After cleaning, use a soft cloth or a polishing cloth to polish the jewelry. This will remove any remaining tarnish and leave it looking shiny and polished.\n\n4. Store the jewelry properly: After cleaning, store the jewelry in a dry, cool place. If possible, keep it in a jewelry box or a cloth bag to protect it from further tarnishing.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify common types of tarnished jewelry and their materials.\nExamine common cleaning methods used for each type of jewelry material.\nIdentify common types of tarnished jewelry and their materials.\n\nAnswer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the type of jewelry: Determine if the jewelry is made of gold, silver, or another material that can tarnish.\n\n2. Choose the appropriate cleaning solution:\n   - For silver: Use a mixture of baking soda and water. Mix one part baking soda with two parts water to create a paste. Apply the paste to the tarnished areas and let it sit for 15-20 minutes.\n   - For gold: Use a mixture of lemon juice and water. Mix equal parts of lemon juice and water in a small bowl. Apply the mixture to the tarnished areas and rub gently with a soft cloth or brush. Rinse with warm water and dry.\n\n3. Polish the jewelry: After cleaning, use a soft cloth or a polishing cloth to polish the jewelry. This will remove any remaining tarnish and leave it looking shiny and polished.\n\n4. Store the jewelry properly: After cleaning, store the jewelry in a dry, cool place. If possible, keep it in a jewelry box or a cloth bag to protect it from further tarnishing.", "time_sec": 27.292, "generation_time_seconds": 24.755, "selection_time_seconds": 2.5266, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 4185, 4494, 315, 30717, 429, 646, 387, 86480, 3304, 323, 1846, 429, 646, 387, 27722, 518, 2114, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.1585, -0.0019, -1.8732, -0.2574, -0.0, -0.4382, -0.2233, -0.2331, -0.1638, -0.2034, -0.0, -0.6206, -4.9857, -0.0, -2.3143, -0.1843, -0.2912, -0.0577, 0.0, -0.0315, -0.0039, -26.4583, -24.8958, -8.7502, -8.137