{"id": "86", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "To prepare a blood slide, you will need a clean glass slide and a drop of blood. Place the slide on a flat surface and add a small drop of blood to one end of the slide. Take another clean slide and touch the blood with one end at a 45-degree angle so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide. Push carefully along the length of the first slide to create a thin smear of blood. Make two smears, allow them to air dry, and label them clearly before placing them in slide transport containers.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. Identify the relevant information in the given passage about preparing blood slides.\n2. Analyze the steps mentioned in the passage for preparing the blood slide.\n3. Extract specific details, such as any required materials, techniques, or precautions mentioned.\n4. Organize the extracted information to form a coherent answer to the question.\n5. Ensure that the answer is based solely on the information provided in the given passage and does not include any external information or assumptions.\n5. Review the extracted information to ensure it accurately reflects the steps and details provided in the passage, without adding any unsupported claims or external knowledge.\n5. Review the extracted information to ensure it accurately reflects the steps and details provided in the passage, without adding any unsupported claims or external knowledge.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 22.187, "generation_time_seconds": 19.0459, "selection_time_seconds": 3.1321, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [5501, 3291, 752, 279, 21085, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645