{"id": "183", "question": "how to cook a small prime rib roast in oven", "gt": "Before cooking the prime rib roast, let it stand at room temperature for at least 1 hour. Preheat the oven to 375 degrees F. Season the roast with a small amount of salt and lots of fresh ground black pepper. Place the roast on a rack in a pan with the rib side down and the fatty side up. Roast it in the oven for 1 hour. After cooking, you can prepare au jus by placing the roasting pan on the stove over high heat. Add wine and cook for 8-10 minutes, stirring and scraping any brown bits. Add beef stock and cook to reduce the juice by half, which might take about 20 minutes. Add salt and pepper to taste.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe given passage does not provide specific instructions on how to cook a small prime rib roast in the oven.\nThe passage does not mention the size of the roast or the oven settings required for cooking.\nThe reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 17.208, "generation_time_seconds": 14.7668, "selection_time_seconds": 2.4343, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 2661, 21085, 1558, 537, 3410, 3151, 11221, 389, 1246, 311, 4296, 264, 2613, 10250, 20131, 57685, 304, 279, 23387, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.4043, -0.9829, -0.0393, -0.0162, -0.0, -0.1454, -0.4058, -0.6173, -0.1281, -0.0044, 0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0013, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0351, 0.0, -0.0085, -0.973, -31.0417, -26.0417, -18.1605, -19.6893, -15.2113, -10.8764, -11.6703, -11.05, -10.8462, -9.8362, -8.2475, -6.6742, -5.8944, -5.5318, -6.0563,