{"id": "240", "question": "how do crab traps work", "gt": "Based on the given passages, a crab trap is a large square metal cage with a system of nets inside that allows crabs to enter through a narrow slit at the top. To set the trap, the ends with lead-ins are placed in the water and the crabs are attracted to the free meal offered by the trap. The Alaska Department of Fish and Game recommends using king crab pots that range from 6 by 6 feet to 8 by 8 feet with heights between 2 and 3 feet. Over time, these mechanisms may disable the trap, preventing it from ghost fishing.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe given passage does not provide information on how crab traps work.\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nThe next logical reasoning step is to determine if there is any external information or context that could provide insight into how crab traps work.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 19.528, "generation_time_seconds": 16.8129, "selection_time_seconds": 2.7073, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 1995, 3897, 304, 279, 21085, 11, 279, 59412, 44560, 975, 553, 279, 2701, 32711, 7354, 1447, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.2781, -0.0, -0.0002, -2.3748, -0.0513, -0.8045, -0.0, -0.2728, -0.0056, -1.3082, -1.2394, -0.361, -0.0602, -0.0125, -8.1889, -0.0143, -2.7746, -0.0015, -0.0589, -Infinity], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_len": 138, "output_tokens": 20, "avg_logp": -Infinity}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [840, 20772, 279, 16953, 315, 279, 59412, 22862, 304, 4285, 3793, 11, 1667, 10295, 323, 35495, 421, 3204, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.7572, -1.6676, -0.2621, -3.0744, -0.0683, -1.0874, -0.0883, -0.0113