{"id": "382", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Passage 3 provides the necessary information to answer the question. To arrange an excel sheet alphabetically, click on the Select All button, switch to the Data tab, locate the Sort & Filter group, click on the Sort option, and then select the desired column to sort by.", "pred": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n1. Open the Excel sheet that you want to arrange alphabetically.\n2. Select the range of cells that you want to sort. You can do this by clicking and dragging over the cells, or by typing the cell range in the formula bar, such as \"A1:C10\" for cells A1 through C10.\n3. Click on the \"Data\" tab in the Excel ribbon at the top of the screen.\n4. In the \"Sort & Filter\" group, click on the \"Sort\" button. This will open the \"Sort\" dialog box.\n5. In the \"Sort\" dialog box, choose whether you want to sort the selected cells by the values in ascending or descending order.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "To arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n1. Open the Excel sheet that you want to arrange alphabetically.\n2. Select the range of cells that you want to sort. You can do this by clicking and dragging over the cells, or by typing the cell range in the formula bar, such as \"A1:C10\" for cells A1 through C10.\n3. Click on the \"Data\" tab in the Excel ribbon at the top of the screen.\n4. In the \"Sort & Filter\" group, click on the \"Sort\" button. This will open the \"Sort\" dialog box.\n5. In the \"Sort\" dialog box, choose whether you want to sort the selected cells by the values in ascending or descending order.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nTo arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n1. Open the Excel sheet that you want to arrange alphabetically.\n2. Select the range of cells that you want to sort. You can do this by clicking and dragging over the cells, or by typing the cell range in the formula bar, such as \"A1:C10\" for cells A1 through C10.\n3. Click on the \"Data\" tab in the Excel ribbon at the top of the screen.\n4. In the \"Sort & Filter\" group, click on the \"Sort\" button. This will open the \"Sort\" dialog box.\n5. In the \"Sort\" dialog box, choose\nChoose whether you want to sort the selected cells by the values in ascending or descending order.\n\nTo arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically, follow these steps:\n1. Open the Excel sheet that you want to arrange alphabetically.\n2. Select the range of cells that you want to sort. You can do this by clicking and dragging over the cells, or by typing the cell range in the formula bar, such as \"A1:C10\" for cells A1 through C10.\n3. Click on the \"Data\" tab in the Excel ribbon at the top of the screen.\n4. In the \"Sort & Filter\" group, click on the \"Sort\" button. This will open the \"Sort\" dialog box.\n5. In the \"Sort\" dialog box, choose whether you want to sort the selected cells by the values in ascending or descending order.", "time_sec": 35.39, "generation_time_seconds": 31.9826, "selection_time_seconds": 3.398, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [25139, 287, 3019, 220, 17, 25, 64547, 279, 1714, 315, 76118, 279, 10834, 27790, 2673, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-7.2957, -0.0028, -0.1834, -0.7102, -0.6169, -0.0097, -0.1374, -0.0062, -1.8386, -2.7172, -