{"id": "422", "question": "what is a upc description", "gt": "A UPC description refers to the Universal Product Code, a barcode symbology used extensively in multiple countries including the United States, Canada, United Kingdom, Australia, New Zealand, and in Europe. It is used for tracking trade items in stores. UPC consists of 12 numeric digits that are uniquely assigned to each trade item. It is primarily used for scanning of trade items at the point of sale, as per GS1 specifications.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe given passage does not contain sufficient information to answer the question about what an UPC description is.\nOutput: Unable to answer based on given passages.\nThe given passage does not contain sufficient information to answer the question about what an UPC description is.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 19.174, "generation_time_seconds": 16.8436, "selection_time_seconds": 2.3191, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [17075, 311, 4226, 3118, 389, 2661, 46769, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.6829, 0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0002, -0.0, -0.0021, -0.0, -28.3333, -26.0417, -15.7623, -9.1722, -10.4191, -8.9687, -7.3355, -6.3051, -6.3055, -6.3723, -6.9625, -6.9526, -6.0247, -4.962, -3.7676, -2.764, -2.0557, -3.3493, -4.451, -5.9641, -6.7591, -6.9219, -4.5945, -4.3234, -4.9208, -5.2642], "cumulative_logprob": -207.7385, "norm_logp": -5.9354, "input_len": 139, "output_tokens": 35, "avg_logp": -5.9353837966918945}, {"beam": 0, "rollo