{"id": "628", "question": "how to guard a tall person in basketball", "gt": "To guard a tall person in basketball, you can stay as close as possible to them near the three-point line, actively slide your feet from side to side to stay near your opponent, and minimize shot opportunities. Additionally, you can keep a wedge between the basket and the offensive player and defend against them with tips from an experienced basketball player.", "pred": "Guarding a tall player in basketball requires understanding their physical attributes, adjusting your stance and positioning, and utilizing your wingspan and arm length. To effectively guard a tall player, maintain a defensive stance with your feet shoulder-width apart, knees slightly bent, and body angled towards the basket. Use your wingspan and arm length to block their shots and passes, keeping your hands up and ready to react quickly.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Guarding a tall player in basketball requires understanding their physical attributes, adjusting your stance and positioning, and utilizing your wingspan and arm length. To effectively guard a tall player, maintain a defensive stance with your feet shoulder-width apart, knees slightly bent, and body angled towards the basket. Use your wingspan and arm length to block their shots and passes, keeping your hands up and ready to react quickly.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Understanding the physical attributes of a tall player.\nTo effectively guard a tall player, it is essential to understand their physical attributes. Tall players typically have longer limbs, making it easier for them to block shots and pass the ball. They may also have a higher jumping ability, allowing them to reach for rebounds and block shots.\nStep 2: Adjusting your stance and positioning.\nWhen guarding a tall player, it's crucial to maintain a defensive stance that allows you to block their path and prevent them from easily getting to the basket. Position yourself with your feet shoulder-width apart and knees slightly bent to maintain balance and agility. Keep your body angled towards the basket to anticipate the tall player's moves.\nStep 3: Utilizing your wingspan and arm length.\nTo guard a tall player, utilize your wingspan and arm length to block their shots and passes. Stay close to the tall player but maintain a proper distance to avoid being easily blocked by their arm movements. Use your arms to block shots and passes, keeping your hands up and ready to react quickly.\n\nAnswer: Guarding a tall player in basketball requires understanding their physical attributes, adjusting your stance and positioning, and utilizing your wingspan and arm length. To effectively guard a tall player, maintain a defensive stance with your feet shoulder-width apart, knees slightly bent, and body angled towards the basket. Use your wingspan and arm length to block their shots and passes, keeping your hands up and ready to react quickly.", "time_sec": 49.825, "generation_time_seconds": 45.999, "selection_time_seconds": 3.8173, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 35386, 323, 43567, 315, 697, 14704, 594, 16217, 76623, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.7641, -0.0016, -0.0808, -3.5725, -0.0057, -0.0005, -0.0004, -6.094, -1.4584, -0.2743, -0.2488, -0.0201, -0.