{"id": "645", "question": "how to plant a potato that has sprouted", "gt": "To plant a sprouted potato, cut it into chunks with two or three eyes each. Place the potato chunks on a tray or cookie sheet and let them dry out overnight. Dig a trench about 4 inches wide and 6 to 8 inches deep in a prepared planting area. Place the sprouted or eye side of the potato chunks facing up, separating each chunk by about 6 to 8 inches. Cover the potatoes with a layer of compost and then replace the dirt on top. Water the potatoes thoroughly and continue watering regularly when the soil is dry to the touch. Add a 4-inch layer of mulch around the plants to keep the soil cool and maintain moisture.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the sprouted potato to ensure it has healthy shoots and no signs of rot.\nChoose a suitable planting location with well-draining soil and ample sunlight.\nPrepare the planting site by loosening the soil and incorporating organic matter to improve drainage and fertility.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 17.891, "generation_time_seconds": 15.3352, "selection_time_seconds": 2.548, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 8151, 18533, 38734, 15516, 311, 8253, 279, 1850, 21448, 369, 47014, 13, 9192, 369, 279, 8151, 18533, 835, 11, 892, 11136, 702, 279, 29905, 323, 1429, 7881, 8151, 411, 11, 438, 419, 686, 387, 279, 835, 12880, 43954, 979, 38341, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.062, -0.0352, -0.0013, -0.3789, -0.1015, -0.0051, -2.0472, -0.1755, -1.1363, -0.1155, -1.6432, -2.4043, -0.0828, -0.1258, -0.0857, -1.6983, -0.0004, -0.2464, -1.0368, -1.7567, -0.0106, -0.5229, -0.0614, -0.6306, -0.8848, -0.1982, -2.3041, -1.6212, -0.0751, -0.2442, -1.13