{"id": "717", "question": "how to poach an egg using a poachpod", "gt": "To poach an egg using a PoachPod, first, bring a large pot of water to a boil. Lightly oil the silicone PoachPod, then crack an egg and gently slide it into the PoachPod, taking care not to break the yolk. Float the PoachPod in the boiling water, ensuring it remains upright and no water gets inside. Cover the pot with a lid and let the egg cook for about six minutes. After cooking, use a large slotted spoon or tongs to lift the PoachPod out of the hot water. Finally, flip the PoachPod upside down over a plate and gently press on the bottom to release the poached egg onto the plate. The PoachPod can be cleaned in a dishwasher.", "pred": "To poach an egg using a poachpod, follow these steps:", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To poach an egg using a poachpod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Ensure the poachpod is clean and free of any debris or old egg whites.\n2. Fill the poachpod with about 3 inches (7.5 cm) of water, making sure the water level is sufficient to cover the egg.\n3. Place the poachpod in the desired heat source, such as a stovetop burner or a sous-vide machine set to 160°F (71°C).\n4. Crack the egg into the poachpod, ensuring the yolk remains intact and the egg white flows smoothly into the water.\n5. Let the egg poach for about 3-4 minutes, or until the egg whites are set and the yolk is cooked to your desired consistency.\n6. Remove the poachpod from the heat source and gently slide the poached egg out using a spatula or fork.\n7. Serve the poached egg immediately with your preferred accompaniments, such as toast, vegetables, or a sauce.\n\nRemember to clean the poachpod thoroughly after use to maintain its functionality for future poaching sessions.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the poachpod's instructions for proper usage.\nLook up the poachpod's instructions online or in its manual for step-by-step guidance.\nExamine the poachpod's design and features to understand how it facilitates the poaching process.\n\nAnswer: To poach an egg using a poachpod, follow these steps:\n\n1. Ensure the poachpod is clean and free of any debris or old egg whites.\n2. Fill the poachpod with about 3 inches (7.5 cm) of water, making sure the water level is sufficient to cover the egg.\n3. Place the poachpod in the desired heat source, such as a stovetop burner or a sous-vide machine set to 160°F (71°C).\n4. Crack the egg into the poachpod, ensuring the yolk remains intact and the egg white flows smoothly into the water.\n5. Let the egg poach for about 3-4 minutes, or until the egg whites are set and the yolk is cooked to your desired consistency.\n6. Remove the poachpod from the heat source and gently slide the poached egg out using a spatula or fork.\n7. Serve the poached egg immediately with your preferred accompaniments, such as toast, vegetables, or a sauce.\n\nRemember to clean the poachpod thoroughly after use to maintain its functionality for future poaching sessions.", "time_sec": 24.335, "generation_time_seconds": 21.1294, "selection_time_seconds": 3.198, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 1667, 264, 13808, 610, 39073, 11, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.5199, -0.0488, -0.0, -0.0005, 0.0, -0.0003, -0.0001, -1.7528, -0.0041, -2.3901, -0.0023, -0.353, -0.0024, -0.0097, -0.0616, -Infinity, -32.9167, -22.7085], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_len": 144, "output_tokens": 18, "avg_logp": -Infinity}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [840, 20772, 279, 7354, 6398, 304, 1667, 264, 3193, 610, 39073, 311, 3193, 610, 458, 18636, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.0616, -0.9231, -0.2958, -1.7993, -0.3249, -0.0001, -0.1213, -0.0527, -0.0019, -0.0001, -0.0006, -0.0424, -0.0003, 0.0, -0.0011, 0.0, -0.317, -0.000