{"id": "44", "question": "how to get plastic out of clothes dryer", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to remove plastic from a clothes dryer:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper, taking care not to damage the dryer's interior.\n3. Apply 1 to 2 tsp. nail polish remover to a clean cloth, and rub the plastic to dissolve it.\n4. Rub the area with a damp cloth to rinse the nail polish remover.\n5. Mix 1 tsp. liquid laundry soap with 1 cup water. Dip a clean cloth in this solution, and rub the area again.\n6. Rinse well with a cloth dipped in clean water.\n\nIf the plastic does not come off with this method, another option is to use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic until it becomes soft and pliable. Then, attempt to peel it off carefully. However, be aware that this method may not work, and in that case, replacing the drum or the entire dryer may be necessary. It is recommended to call a service technician for this type of repair.\n\nTherefore, the answer to the question of how to get plastic out of clothes dryer is:\n\n1. Run the dryer on a regular setting for 20 minutes to soften the plastic.\n2. Scrape the plastic off with a wooden or plastic spatula or paint scraper.\n3. Apply nail polish remover to dissolve the plastic.\n4. Rinse with a damp cloth and soap solution.\n5. Use a hair dryer or heat gun to heat the plastic if necessary.\n\nIf the plastic still does not come off, consider replacing the drum or the entire dryer.", "pred": "To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first determine the type of plastic that is stuck in the dryer. Then, carefully remove the plastic from the dryer, being careful not to damage the dryer or the plastic itself.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first determine the type of plastic that is stuck in the dryer. Then, carefully remove the plastic from the dryer, being careful not to damage the dryer or the plastic itself.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe steps you have provided are instructions on how to get plastic out of a clothes dryer. The steps include:\nThe first step is to determine the type of plastic that is stuck in the dryer.\nThe second step is to carefully remove the plastic from the dryer, avoiding damaging the dryer or the plastic itself.\n\nAnswer: To get plastic out of a clothes dryer, first determine the type of plastic that is stuck in the dryer. Then, carefully remove the plastic from the dryer, being careful not to damage the dryer or the plastic itself.", "time_sec": 25.866, "generation_time_seconds": 22.5851, "selection_time_seconds": 3.2696, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 2530, 315, 279, 12188, 304, 279, 46622, 624, 8304, 220, 17, 25, 29901, 421, 1052, 525, 894, 9434, 9666, 315, 12188, 304, 279, 46622, 476, 46622, 10378, 624, 8304, 220, 18, 25, 4248, 421, 279, 46622, 702, 894, 13406, 476, 15310, 429, 2578, 614, 17006, 279, 12188, 624, 8304, 220, 19, 25, 9192, 369, 12188, 48132, 476, 33998, 4766, 279, 46622, 23196, 476, 389, 279, 14285, 315, 279, 46622, 624, 8304, 220, 20, 25, 81835, 421, 279, 46622, 702, 894, 13055, 8413, 798, 24140, 476, 46622, 20332, 429, 1231, 614, 827, 396, 47172, 624, 8304, 220, 21, 25, 9726, 987, 279, 17438, 1660, 31620, 311, 5978, 902, 12188, 48674, 614, 1012, 22409, 504, 3681, 20907, 624, 8304, 220, 22, 25, 1416, 279], "logp_list": [-2.3499, -0.0026, -0.0264, -0.0002, -0.1256, -0.0148, -1.2044, -0.0023, -0.1175, -0.1492, -0.3903, -0.0032, -0.252, -0.5361, -0.1481, -0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.1515, -0.3834, -3.5718, -0.2645, -0.0953, -0.2606, -2.4993, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.3016, -0.0001, -0.0007, -2.0331, -2.0084, -0.2082, -0.012, -0.0001, 0.0, -0.0, 0.0, -0.2488, -0.