{"id": "88", "question": "how to prepare blood slide", "gt": "Sure, I'd be happy to help you with that! Here are the steps to prepare a blood slide based on the provided passages:\n\n1. First, sterilize a needle with a flame as described in Passage 1.\n2. Next, obtain a blood sample by pricking your finger or using a blood donation kit. This will require adult supervision, especially if you are doing it yourself.\n3. Place a drop of blood towards one end of a clean glass slide as instructed in Passage 2.\n4. Take another clean slide and, holding it at an angle of about 45 degrees, touch the blood with one end of the slide so that the blood runs along the edge of the slide through capillary action. Gently push the blood along the length of the first slide to produce a thin smear of blood. Repeat this step to make two smears.\n5. Allow the smears to air dry completely before labeling them clearly and placing them in the provided slide transport containers as suggested in Passage 3.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\n1. Identify the relevant information in the given passage about preparing blood slides.\n2. Analyze the steps mentioned in the passage for preparing the blood slide.\n3. Extract specific details, such as any required materials, techniques, or precautions mentioned.\n4. Organize the extracted information to form a coherent answer to the question.\n5. Ensure that the answer is based solely on the information provided in the given passage and does not include any external information or assumptions.\n5. Review the extracted information to ensure it accurately reflects the steps and details provided in the passage, without adding any unsupported claims or ext