{"id": "172", "question": "how to soften sugar", "gt": "To soften sugar, place brown sugar in a plastic container with a small piece of plastic wrap or foil over the sugar. Put a damp paper towel or napkin on top of the plastic/foil. Cover tightly. Remove damp paper towel in a couple of days. Alternatively, preheat oven to lowest temperature (150-200 degrees) and remove sugar from package. Put in an ovenproof container and place in the warm oven for 15 minutes. Tap sugar with a spoon and if it starts to fall apart, turn oven off and leave sugar in the oven for an hour or two to completely dry out. Store granulated sugar in an airtight container and confectioners sugar in a cool, dry location.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe passage does not provide any specific methods for softening sugar.\nSince the passage does not provide any specific methods for softening sugar, I cannot provide a method based on the given information.\nThe passage does not provide any specific methods for softening sugar.\nSince the passage does not provide any specific methods for softening sugar, I cannot provide a method based on the given information.\nThe passage does not mention any chemical reactions or temperature changes that could soften sugar.\nSince the passage does not mention any chemical reactions or temperature changes that could soften sugar, I cannot provide a method based on the given information.\nThe passage does not provide any information about the physical properties of sugar that could be altered to soften it.\nSince the passage does not provide any information about the physical properties of sugar that could be altered to soften it, I cannot provide\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 21.322, "generation_time_seconds": 18.5472, "s