{"id": "295", "question": "what is the proper way to fertilize your grass", "gt": "Based on the given passages, the proper way to fertilize your grass is to:\n\n1. Fertilize at the right time of year, which is at the beginning of the growing season, and varies for different types of grasses.\n2. Choose a fertilizer that is suitable for your type of grass and soil pH, as determined by a soil test.\n3. Apply the fertilizer in a perpendicular pattern, avoiding over-fertilization, which can be determined by checking if the leaf blades bounce back up after being stepped on.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the type of grass you have and whether it is a perennial or annual variety.\nResearch the specific fertilization needs of your grass type, considering factors such as soil composition, climate, and growing conditions.\nDetermine the appropriate time of year to apply the fertilizer based on the grass type, typically during the growing season when the grass is actively growing.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 18.021, "generation_time_seconds": 15.5236, "selection_time_seconds": 2.4863, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.0493, -1.021, -0.0289, -0.0236, -0.5767, -Infinity, -33.2292, -23.3333, -14.3985, -17.1291, -15.8424, -14.2885, -14.4446, -14.4423, -13.3051, -13.1476, -12.5149, -12.3062, -10.3712], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_len": 143, "output_tokens": 19, "avg_logp": -Infinity}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 943, 315, 16359, 498, 614, 323, 