{"id": "339", "question": "how to make ribs", "gt": "To make ribs, start by removing the membrane from the bottom of the ribs. Then, brush both sides of the ribs with a mixture of mustard and liquid smoke. Sprinkle the ribs with a dry rub and pat gently to ensure it sticks to the meat. Next, heat a gas or charcoal grill to medium and place the ribs on the grill, meaty-side up. Brush the ribs with sauce, cover the grill, and cook for 5 minutes. Flip the ribs, brush with more sauce, and cook for another 5 minutes. Repeat this process, flipping and brushing every 5 minutes, until the sauce thickens and the ribs are heated through with grill marks, for a total grilling time of 20 minutes.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the specific type of ribs to be prepared and their preparation method.\nIdentify the specific type of ribs to be prepared and their preparation method.\nSince the given passage only provides a general statement about making ribs without specific instructions, the next logical step would be to search for or provide a more detailed recipe or method for preparing ribs.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 21.957, "generation_time_seconds": 19.2846, "selection_time_seconds": 2.6627, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1887, 13966, 4362, 369, 3259, 55149, 624, 12, 45302, 11, 279, 1887, 13966, 369, 3259, 55149, 2924, 55149, 320, 461, 1279, 504, 264, 23694, 476, 264, 19362, 701, 12021, 11, 24353, 11, 323, 264, 10273, 476, 89115, 1021, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.7038, -0.003, -0.0205