{"id": "361", "question": "What’s the difference between ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy?", "gt": "The main difference between ad hominem fallacy and poisoning the well fallacy is the timing of the attack. Ad hominem fallacy attacks the person making the argument instead of attacking the argument directly, but poisoning the well fallacy is a preemptive attack on a person's character or integrity before they have even made their argument. In other words, ad hominem fallacy is a reaction to an argument, while poisoning the well fallacy is a preemptive strike to discredit an opponent before they have a chance to present their argument.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe reasoning steps are:\nTo determine the difference between the ad hominem fallacy and the poisoning the well fallacy, we need to analyze the logical structure and intent of each.\nThe next logical reasoning step is to examine the specific examples and definitions provided in the passage to understand how each fallacy operates:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 29.689, "generation_time_seconds": 26.1213, "selection_time_seconds": 3.5573, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 32711, 7354, 525, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.5583, -0.3863, -0.0354, -0.0257, -0.5113, -Infinity, -32.5, -26.0417, -17.975, -15.9615, -14.5547, -13.1557, -13.3798, -13.9791, -12.5208, -12.7125, -11.6676, -11.6703, -10.0355, -8.2042, -7.3131, -7.2958, -7.0874, -6.6928, -7.5454, -7.035], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_