{"id": "410", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Torn pieces of bread are pushed through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n3. The crumbs are spread on a baking sheet.\n4. The sheet is baked in the preheated oven until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n5. The sheet is shaken twice during baking to ensure even drying.\n6. After baking, the crumbs are removed from the oven and allowed to cool completely.\n\nAlternatively, according to passage 2, you can also make panko crumbs by:\n\n1. Pushing chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to create coarse crumbs.\n2. Spreading the crumbs on a baking sheet and baking at 300 degrees F until the crumbs are dry but not toasted, for 6 to 8 minutes.\n3. Shaking the sheet twice during baking.\n4. Being careful not to let the crumbs brown.\n\nFinally, passage 3 provides a third method for making panko crumbs, which involves blending the ingredients in a blender carafe and baking them on half sheet pans until they are crisp and lightly browned.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the ingredients and tools needed for making panko crumbs.\nExamine the method of preparing the panko crumbs, including the steps and techniques involved.\nExamine the specific techniques and tools used in preparing panko crumbs, such as how to properly toast or bake the bread before crumbing it.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 18.437, "generation_time_seconds": 15.8372, "selection_time_seconds": 2.5892, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids"