{"id": "497", "question": "salary exchange pension contributions", "gt": "Based on the given passages, it appears that salary exchange is a way for employees to give up part of their salary in exchange for a pension contribution made by their employer. The salary that is waived is equal to the value of the employee's regular pension contribution, minus any additional contributions. The employer then pays the corresponding amount into the relevant pension scheme. This arrangement allows both employers and employees to potentially save money through reduced national insurance contributions.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the specific types of pension contributions mentioned in the passage.\nLook for any examples or comparisons provided in the passage that relate to salary exchange pension contributions.\nLook for any specific examples or comparisons in the passage that relate to salary exchange pension contributions.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 18.214, "generation_time_seconds": 15.5877, "selection_time_seconds": 2.6196, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 3151, 4494, 315, 27681, 19026, 9733, 304, 279, 21085, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.9084, -0.0006, -0.0383, -0.599, -3.1458, -0.0141, -0.4385, -0.0014, -0.1532, -0.0228, -0.00