{"id": "530", "question": "how does ez pass charges work", "gt": "Sure! Based on the given passages, here is how E-ZPass charging works:\n\nWhen you sign up for E-ZPass, a certain amount is charged to your credit card to establish a balance (specifically, $100 for the EZ-Tag and $25 for the TX-Tag). This balance is used to pay for tolls as you drive through toll lanes. When you drive through a toll booth, the toll tag mounted on your windshield is read by the antennae, and your E-ZPass account is charged the appropriate amount. The amount is deducted from your balance. If your balance falls below a certain threshold ($10 for the TX-Tag), E-ZPass will charge your credit card an additional $100 or $25 to top up your balance.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the passage for any specific examples or mechanisms described for how EZ Pass charges work.\nIdentify if there are any costs or fees mentioned related to the operation of the EZ Pass system.\nExamine the passage for any specific examples or mechanisms described for how EZ Pass charges work, focusing on the technical aspects and any costs associated with using the system.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 22.769, "generation_time_seconds": 19.5186, "selection_time_seconds": 3.242, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [840, 19991, 279, 10431, 315, 63286, 9970, 304, 3151, 5302, 476, 13604, 369, 11682, 10295, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.4832, -0.1174, -0.0177, -7.662, -0.421, -0.4021, -1.0238, -0.5208, -3.5751, -1.0551, -0.3825, -0.1641, -2.8828, -1.5362, -0.0526, -0.3652, -0.0003, -27.5, -19.584