{"id": "705", "question": "what do children learn with water play", "gt": "Based on the given passages, children learn the following through water play:\n\n1. Gross motor skills: Running, pouring, and manipulating water helps develop fine and gross motor skills. (Passage 1)\n2. Science concepts: Floating and sinking, measurement, and experimentation with different objects in water. (Passage 1)\n3. Creativity and imagination: Water play encourages children to use their imagination and engage in pretend play. (Passage 1)\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not mention any other specific academic learning outcomes beyond gross motor skills, science concepts, and creativity.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe passages state that children learn with water play. They do not specify what exactly they learn.\nThe passages do not provide specific examples, numbers, or comparisons regarding what children learn with water play.\nThe passages do not include any supporting details about what children learn with water play, such as specific skills or knowledge gained.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 22.678, "generation_time_seconds": 19.9337, "selection_time_seconds": 2.7353, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28715, 389, 279, 2661, 21085, 11, 2841, 3960, 1526, 3015, 1486, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.8027, -0.0001, -0.0003, -0.1844, -0.2892, -0.0078, -0.8946, -0.0998, -1.3715, -0.0007, -0.0, -0.7287, -0.6205, -33.3333, -28.3333, -12.2972, -13.3403, -9.8347, -10.2873, -8.5949, -7.5018, -