{"id": "138", "question": "what is the treatment when asset is discarded as per income tax act", "gt": "Based on the Income Tax Act, when an asset is discarded but not sold, the scrap value of the asset can be reduced from the block in the previous year in which the asset is discarded as per section 43(6). This is done under the block concept, where all assets of the same class and subject to the same rate of depreciation are considered as a single asset. Any changes to the block's value must abide by the provisions of Chapter IV D of the Income Tax Act, 1961. Additionally, the assessee can claim depreciation on the residual value of such discarded asset, even if it's not used for the purposes of business or profession in that year and subsequent years.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExamine the specific provisions of the Income Tax Act related to the disposal of assets for treatment purposes.\nLook up the specific sections of the Income Tax Act that deal with the treatment of assets when they are discarded.\nLook up the specific sections of the Income Tax Act that deal with the treatment of assets when they are discarded.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 21.65, "generation_time_seconds": 18.4481, "selection_time_seconds": 3.1918, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 1376, 5424, 315, 279, 3405, 13, 576, 3405, 374, 10161, 911, 279, 6380, 315, 458, 9329, 979, 432, 374, 43210, 4092, 311, 279, 32520, 15190, 3218, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.1324, -0.0014, -0.0332, -0.0003, -0.0789, -0.01, -1.8589, -1.2943, -0.0579, -0.0, -0.0035, -1.4334, -0.016, -0.0305, -0.9234, -0.0648, -0.0047, 