{"id": "252", "question": "how to grill pork chops, allrecipes.com", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com:\n\n1. Preheat an outdoor grill for medium heat, and lightly oil the grate. (Passage 1)\n2. In a bowl, mix together seasoned salt, black pepper, garlic powder, onion powder, paprika, Worcestershire sauce, and smoke flavoring until thoroughly combined. Rinse pork chops, and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. (Passage 1)\n3. For Oven-Fried Pork Chops, use stuffing mix for the breading. The pork chops come out tender and juicy. This recipe takes 30 minutes to prepare and 10 minutes to prep. (Passage 2)\n4. To grill pork chops over indirect heat, rinse the chops and sprinkle the wet chops on both sides with the spice mixture. Massage the spice rub into the meat for 10 minutes before grilling. Grill the chops until no longer pink inside, about 12 minutes per side. (Passage 3)\n\nTherefore, to grill pork chops according to Allrecipes.com, you should preheat the grill, season the pork chops with a spice mixture, and grill them over indirect heat until they are cooked through.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.\nThe question asks for instructions on how to grill pork chops from Allrecipes.com. The given passage does not contain any information about grilling pork chops or provide any links to Allrecipes.com or related recipes. Therefore, the available information is insufficient to answer the question.\nGiven the lack of specific information about grilling pork chops and the absence of any reference to Allrecipes.com, it is clear that the passages do not provide the necessary details to answer the question accurately.\n\nUnable to ans