{"id": "283", "question": "difference between an adverb clause and an adjective clause", "gt": "Based on the given passages, an adverb clause modifies a verb, adjective or another adverb, while an adjective clause modifies a noun or pronoun.", "pred": "The main difference between adverb clauses and adjective clauses is that adverb clauses modify verbs, adjectives, or other adverb clauses, while adjective clauses modify nouns or pronouns.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Adverb clauses are used to modify verbs, adjectives, or other adverb clauses. They are typically introduced by adverbs and can modify any part of the sentence. For example, in the sentence \"I walked slowly down the street,\" the adverb \"slowly\" modifies the verb \"walked.\"\n\nAdjective clauses are used to modify nouns or pronouns. They are typically introduced by relatives and can modify any part of the sentence. For example, in the sentence \"The book that I read last night was interesting,\" the adjective clause \"that I read last night\" modifies the noun \"book.\"\n\nThe main difference between adverb clauses and adjective clauses is that adverb clauses modify verbs, adjectives, or other adverb clauses, while adjective clauses modify nouns or pronouns.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nExplain the function of adverb clauses and adjective clauses in a sentence.\nIdentify the structure of adverb clauses and adjective clauses in a sentence.\nExplain how adverb clauses modify verbs, adjectives, or other adverb clauses.\n\nAdverb clauses are used to modify verbs, adjectives, or other adverb clauses. They are typically introduced by adverbs and can modify any part of the sentence. For example, in the sentence \"I walked slowly down the street,\" the adverb \"slowly\" modifies the verb \"walked.\"\n\nAdjective clauses are used to modify nouns or pronouns. They are typically introduced by relatives and can modify any part of the sentence. For example, in the sentence \"The book that I read last night was interesting,\" the adjective clause \"that I read last night\" modifies the noun \"book.\"\n\nThe main difference between adverb clauses and adjective clauses is that adverb clauses modify verbs, adjectives, or other adverb clauses, while adjective clauses modify nouns or pronouns.", "time_sec": 29.27, "generation_time_seconds": 26.3829, "selection_time_seconds": 2.8776, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 1156, 3019, 374, 311, 23643, 279, 2661, 1995, 911, 993, 22328, 49098, 323, 84492, 49098, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.7682, -3.5446, -0.2022, -0.164, -0.0023, -2.1464, -0.0051, -0.3407, -3.2042, -1.4502, -0.1557, -0.0013, -0.0036, -0.0003, -0.0003, 0.0, -0.3269, -0.1959, -28.75, -26.0417, -14.732, -11.9689, -13.959, -10.8346, -10.2113, -9.8108, -11.2605, -10.8494, -8.3787], "cumulative_logprob": -170.3088, "norm_logp": -5.8727, "input_len": 143, "output_tokens": 29, "avg_logp": -5.872713565826416}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [2082, 993, 22328, 21647, 82949, 264, 18607, 11, 84492, 11, 476, 2441, 993, 22328, 11, 8241, 1995, 911, 279, 1917, 11, 882, 11, 1992, 11, 476, 11566, 13, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.664, -0.0708, -0.0, -0.0012, -0.1489, -0.0215, -0.0016, -0.004, -0.6328, -0.0003, -0.0002, -0.2856, -0.0, 0.0, -0.5287, -0.7634, -0.0236, -0.0529, -2.2158, -2.1022, -0.0857, -1.4025, -0.0, -0.0936, -0.0, -2.8307, -0.0064, -0.1089, -1.8264], "cumulative_logprob": -14.8717, "norm_logp": -0.5128, "input_len": 143, "output_tokens": 29, "avg_logp": -0.5128093957901001}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 2, "token_ids": [785, 32711, 7354, 525, 25, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 