{"id": "304", "question": "what causes watermelons to explode", "gt": "Watermelons can explode due to external pressure, such as when a bunch of rubber bands are placed around the middle of the watermelon, causing potential energy to build up and eventually cause the watermelon to explode. Another cause of watermelon explosions is the buildup of gas inside the watermelon due to rotting. This increases the internal pressure and when the skin of the watermelon can no longer hold the gas inside, it will explode.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the conditions under which watermelons are most likely to explode.\nAnalyze the physical properties of watermelons that could lead to an explosion.\nExamine the internal structure and composition of watermelons that can contribute to an explosion.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 18.855, "generation_time_seconds": 16.5868, "selection_time_seconds": 2.2606, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 1156, 3019, 374, 311, 10542, 279, 3151, 3565, 304, 279, 21085, 429, 3410, 1995, 911, 1128, 11137, 3015, 27127, 2382, 311, 15758, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.9665, -3.3828, -0.3084, -0.3005, -0.0017, -0.2342, -0.0402, -2.3902, -0.6554, -1.9026, -0.0, -0.2282, -0.0317, -5.0289, -0.0754, -0.0443, -0.6031, -0.0026, -0.0001, -0.0, 0.0, -0.0, -0.0011, -0.0032, -0.2158, -30.625, -22.7083, -13.6062, -10.3647, -11.8434, -11.6682, -11.0427, -9.5904, -12.7096, -11.2621, -11.4739,