{"id": "329", "question": "how to boil potatoes for easy peeling", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here's how to boil potatoes for easy peeling:\n\nPassage 1 recommends boiling the potatoes until they are tender, then transferring them to an ice water bath to stop the cooking process. After cooling, the skin can be easily peeled off. This method takes 15 minutes to cook the potatoes and 5 seconds to peel each one.\n\nPassage 2 suggests peeling the potatoes before cooking, as their skin can be tough and papery. However, no specific instructions are provided for peeling.\n\nPassage 3 provides a step-by-step guide for peeling cooked potatoes. The method involves scoring the potatoes all the way around the center, boiling them for about 15 minutes, then placing them in an ice water bath to cool. Once cooled, the skin can be easily removed. This method takes about 30 minutes total time.\n\nTherefore, based on the provided passages, the best way to boil potatoes for easy peeling is to boil them until tender, then transfer them to an ice water bath to stop the cooking process and make the skin easier to remove. Scoring the potatoes before boiling can also help loosen the skin for easier peeling.", "pred": "To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first boil the potatoes until they are tender but not too soft. Once the potatoes are tender, drain them and let them cool for a few minutes. Gently peel the potatoes from the top downwards, starting at the top to avoid damaging the meat of the potato.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first boil the potatoes until they are tender but not too soft. Once the potatoes are tender, drain them and let them cool for a few minutes. Gently peel the potatoes from the top downwards, starting at the top to avoid damaging the meat of the potato.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nStep 1: Boil the potatoes until they are tender but not too soft. This ensures the skins can be easily removed.\nStep 2: Once the potatoes are tender, drain them and let them cool for a few minutes. This makes the skins easier to remove.\nStep 3: Gently peel the potatoes from the top downwards, using your fingers or a potato peeler. Start at the top and work your way down to avoid damaging the meat of the potato.\n\nAnswer: To boil potatoes for easy peeling, first boil the potatoes until they are tender but not too soft. Once the potatoes are tender, drain them and let them cool for a few minutes. Gently peel the potatoes from the top downwards, starting at the top to avoid damaging the meat of the potato.", "time_sec": 27.051, "generation_time_seconds": 23.7418, "selection_time_seconds": 3.2995, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [1249, 43690, 34167, 369, 4135, 1051, 20058, 11, 498, 1184, 311, 1795, 1493, 7354, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.0418, -0.3547, -0.0, -0.0068, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0014, -2.6411, -1.0473, -0.0001, -0.53, -0.313, -0.0033, -0.0625, -Infinity, -31.4583, -21.2507, -17.3948, -18.2094, -12.3354, -9.4998, -10.2824, -9.2682, -8.8188, -9.2222, -9.8007, -8.9683, -8.1486, -6.715, -5.2089, -3.8573, -3.2033, -2.0083, -2.494, -3.2611, -4.0726, -4.7601, -5.3878, -5.9273, -5.2665, -4.836, -4.7749, -5.964, -6.5056, -5.9622, -5.1492, -3.9445, -4.7064, -5.6895, -6.3631], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_len": 141, "output_tokens": 51, "avg_logp": -Infinity}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [22043, 279, 3019, 14319, 29208, 32711, 11, 279, 1790, 19819, 3019, 374, 311, 3410, 264, 1714, 476, 14762, 369, 49837, 34167, 429, 