{"id": "364", "question": "how to get antique effect on wood using normal paint", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here are some steps to achieve an antique effect on wood using normal paint:\n\n1. Apply a basecoat of flat or satin paint to the wood surface ( passage 3). Satin paint is easier to work with, but flat paint will give a more aged look.\n2. Mix paint that is two shades darker than the basecoat with an equal amount of glaze ( passage 3). Once the basecoat is dry, drizzle a crumpled rag or plastic bag in the glaze mixture to achieve an aged appearance.\n3. Layer stain on top of the paint to create a cool effect ( passage 1). This technique involves applying multiple layers of stain and allowing them to dry between coats.\n4. Use a palette knife to spread a mixture of molding paste and a rust or dull color on a canvas, letting it dry before adding additional layers ( passage 2). This can help create an embossed design with an antique finish.\n5. Apply a thin layer of burnt sienna or a similar color to give the wood a vintage look ( passage 3). Dabbing the paint with a paper towel or cloth can help remove excess paint and achieve a more subtle, aged appearance.\n\nOverall, the key to achieving an antique effect on wood using normal paint is to layer different materials and colors to create a weathered and worn appearance.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe question asks how to achieve an antique effect on wood using normal paint. To answer this, we need to consider the following steps:\nStep 1: Identify the characteristics of an antique effect on wood.\nAn antique effect on wood typically includes a weathered appearance, a darker or aged color, and possibly a distressed texture. These characteristics are often achieved through specific techniques and materials.\nStep 2: Determine the techniques and materials required to create an antique effect on wood using normal paint.\nTo create an antique effect on wood using normal paint, techniques such as layering different colors of paint, applying texture overlays, and using a glaze or varnish to create a distressed appearance can be employed. Materials such as paintbrushes, rollers, and sandpaper may also be necessary for achieving the desired effect.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 40.881, "generation_time_seconds": 37.4297, "selection_time_seconds": 3.4394, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 3405, 17064, 1246, 311, 11075, 458, 46591, 2456, 389, 7579, 1667, 4622, 6177, 13, 2014, 4226, 419, 11, 582, 1184, 311, 2908, 279, 2701, 7354, 1447, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-0.9771, -0.8899, -0.0203, -0.7292, 0.0, -0.0569, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0, -0.0001, -0.0492, -0.0003, -0.0529, -0.2684, -0.5026, -0.0059, -0.0062, -0.129, -0.0141, -0.0014, -0.3292, -0.3429, -2.6791, -0.0505, -0.0305, -Infinity, -33.0208, -21.6667, -10.7578, -8.5776, -20.6261, -12.3077, -9.8296, -8.8341, -9.6316, -8.5198, -9.0596, -8.1142, -8.0829, -6.8287, -5.3078, -4.1385, -3.5896, -3.2807, -4.6896, -6.1181, -6.9932, -7.1618, -7.7714, -7.7599, -6.9952], "cumulative_logprob": -Infinity, "norm_logp": -Infinity, "input_len": 143, "output_tokens": 53, "avg_logp": -Infinity}, {"beam": 0, "rollout": 1, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 7236, 4362, 369, 31045, 458, 46591, 2456, 389, 7579, 1667, 4622, 6177, 13, 1096, 5646, 279, 943, 315, 6177, 11, 279, 7375, 2567, 11, 323, 894, 5107, 7236, 1741, 438, 61626, 11, 88613, 11, 476, 22899, 42632, 382, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 