{"id": "384", "question": "how to arrange an excel sheet alphabetical", "gt": "Based on the provided passages, here is how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically:\n\nPassage 1 suggests using Kutools for Excel, which provides a Sort Sheets tool to easily sort all worksheets in alphabetical order. However, if you prefer not to use macros or Kutools, Passage 2 provides an alternative method using the built-in Sort feature in Excel.\n\nTo sort an Excel sheet alphabetically using the built-in Sort feature, follow these steps:\n\n1. Select the data you wish to sort by clicking on the Select All button at the intersection of your row and column headings.\n2. Switch to the Data tab in the Microsoft Excel ribbon and locate the Sort & Filter group.\n3. Click on the Sort option.\n4. Click on the Sort By drop-down menu and select the column you wish to sort by (e.g., Product column in alphabetical order - A to Z).\n5. Click OK.\n\nOnce you have completed these steps, the data in your Excel sheet will be sorted alphabetically.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages. The passages do not provide sufficient information to clarify how to arrange an Excel sheet numerically.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe question asks how to arrange an Excel sheet alphabetically. To address this, we need to consider the steps involved in organizing data in Excel.\nThe reasoning steps are:\nWe need to look for information in the given passages about sorting Excel sheets alphabetically.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 31.97, "generation_time_seconds": 28.8311, "selection_time_seconds": 3.1303, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 279, 21085, 429, 5610, 1995, 389, 76