{"id": "411", "question": "how to make panko crumbs", "gt": "Sure, I can help you with that! Based on the given passages, here's a step-by-step guide on how to make panko crumbs:\n\n1. Preheat the oven to 300 degrees F (150 degrees C).\n2. Push torn pieces of bread or chunks of white bread through the shredding disk of a food processor to make coarse crumbs.\n3. Spread the crumbs on a baking sheet.\n4. Bake in preheated oven until crumbs are dry but not toasted, 6 to 8 minutes. Shake the sheet twice during baking to evenly dry the crumbs.\n5. Remove from the oven and cool completely.\n\nIf you want to store the panko crumbs for later use, you can transfer them to an airtight container and keep them at room temperature for up to 2 weeks.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any further questions.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nIdentify the ingredients typically used in making panko crumbs.\nIdentify the specific method or technique used to prepare panko crumbs.\nExamine the preparation method described in the passages, focusing on the steps involved in creating panko crumbs.\n\nAnswer: Unable to answer based on given passages.", "time_sec": 20.172, "generation_time_seconds": 17.4384, "selection_time_seconds": 2.7263, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [8304, 220, 16, 25, 64547, 13966, 323, 7375, 4362, 369, 3259, 281, 92852, 96577, 624, 785, 46769, 1265, 3410, 1995, 389, 279, 3151, 13966, 2567, 320, 5464, 398, 16002, 11, 19828, 11, 323, 7025, 48559, 476, 3200, 819, 8, 323, 894, 7375, 4362, 320, 4803, 264, 3607, 17654, 476, 264, 20097, 8983, 3593], "logp_list": [-2.9897, -0.0035, -0.0585, -0.0004, -0.2112, -8.3453, -1.8841, -0.1674, -0.2327, -0.4865, -0.0061, -0.0005, -0.0, -0.