: "success"}}
{"id": "434", "question": "how to clean tarnished jewelry at home", "gt": "Based on the given passages, here's a brief answer to the question \"How to clean tarnished jewelry at home\":\n\nTo clean tarnished jewelry at home, mix a few drops of mild dish soap with warm water and dip a soft cloth in the solution. Rub the jewelry gently, then rinse it in cool water and buff it with a cloth until dry. For heavier tarnish, mix a paste of three parts baking soda to one part water and apply it with a soft, lint-free cloth. You can also use a saltwater solution by pouring two cups of hot water into a bowl and submerging the jewelry in it. Let it sit for a while, then remove and rinse it with cool water. Be sure to use a soft-bristle brush or old toothbrush to clean diamonds.", "pred": "To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first identify the type of metal in your jewelry. For gold, use a mixture of equal parts baking soda and water in a small bowl. For silver, you'll need silver polish and a soft cloth or sponge. Ensure your hands are clean before handling the jewelry to avoid introducing oils and dirt. Prepare the cleaning solution or polish as directed, and clean the jewelry accordingly.", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Answer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first identify the type of metal in your jewelry. For gold, use a mixture of equal parts baking soda and water in a small bowl. For silver, you'll need silver polish and a soft cloth or sponge. Ensure your hands are clean before handling the jewelry to avoid introducing oils and dirt. Prepare the cleaning solution or polish as directed, and clean the jewelry accordingly.", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nFirst, identify the type of metal in your jewelry. Different metals require different cleaning methods. For example, gold can be cleaned with a mixture of baking soda and water, while silver might need a solution of silver polish and water.\nSecond, gather the appropriate cleaning materials. For gold jewelry, you can use a mixture of equal parts baking soda and water in a small bowl. For silver, you'll need silver polish and a soft cloth or sponge. Ensure your hands are clean before handling the jewelry to avoid introducing oils and dirt.\nThird, prepare the cleaning solution or polish. Mix the baking soda and water for gold or apply silver polish as directed. Make sure the solution or polish is safe for the type of metal you are cleaning.\n\nAnswer: To clean tarnished jewelry at home, first identify the type of metal in your jewelry. For gold, use a mixture of equal parts baking soda and water in a small bowl. For silver, you'll need silver polish and a soft cloth or sponge. Ensure your hands are clean before handling the jewelry to avoid introducing oils and dirt. Prepare the cleaning solution or polish as directed, and clean the jewelry accordingly.", "time_sec": 27.937, "generation_time_seconds": 25.1185, "selection_time_seconds": 2.8098, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [785, 32711, 3019, 374, 25, 64547, 279, 943, 315, 9317, 304, 279, 30717, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-1.3669, -1.1878, -3.1684, -0.2836, -0.2826, -0.2417, -0.1763, -0.1118, -0.0024, -0.178, -0.3086, -0.0645, -0.0154, -0.6338, -0.0502, -28.3333, -21.7708, -15.3411, -18.75, -15.0, -14.263, -15.6269, -13.7567, -11.3464, -13.1511, -14.1703, -10.6681, -10.6352, -9.8709, -8.868, -8.8472, -8.2443, -7.9981, -5.8861, -6.5086, -6.4292, -7.0526, -8.4146, -8.4151, -7.9484, -8.1735, -8.3729, -7.4654, -7.828, -7.9849, -7.6648, -7.558], "cumulative_logprob": -360.4155, "norm_logp": -7.6684, "input_len": 141, "output_token