{"id": "518", "question": "how do raffles work", "gt": "Raffles work by selling tickets to participants, who have the opportunity to win prizes. The specific details and mechanics of a raffle can vary. In a reverse raffle, participants purchase tickets with numbers on them, and the last ticket drawn wins the main prize. In a 50-50 draw, tickets are sold during an event, and 50% of the proceeds go to the winner of a random draw, while the other 50% is allocated for a charitable purpose. In some cases, raffles may also offer additional opportunities to win prizes, such as cash tip board raffles.", "pred": "Unable to answer based on given passages", "group_key": "ragtruth", "sub_category": "ragtruth", "dataset": "ragtruth", "method": "base_gd", "raw_output": "Unable to answer based on given passages", "cot": "The reasoning steps are:\n\nThe given passage does not provide any information about how raffles work.\nUnable to answer based on given passages\nThe given passage does not provide any information about how raffles work.\n\nUnable to answer based on given passages", "time_sec": 17.498, "generation_time_seconds": 15.0082, "selection_time_seconds": 2.4796, "record_process": true, "stages": [{"step": 0, "rollouts": [{"beam": 0, "rollout": 0, "token_ids": [28301, 1437, 279, 1376, 6813, 323, 7354, 9733, 304, 279, 2661, 21085, 5435, 311, 1246, 435, 80535, 975, 13, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645, 151645], "logp_list": [-2.0774, -0.0013, -0.0725, -0.2366, -0.4965, -1.7155, -2.0072, -5.8265, -0.006, -0.0002, -2.0711, -0.115, -2.1464, 0.0, -0.0608, -0.0075, -0.0, -0.0029, -0.0077, -0.0037, -31.0417, -26.875, -18.75, -17.709, -9.2842, -7.5968, -5.9787, -5.4758, -6.3068, -6.8537, -6.8962, -6.4032, -5.